{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '27,49p;91,119p;168,192p;323,338p;346,368p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '27,49p;91,119p;168,192p;323,338p;346,368p'\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window\n    27\t## Authority and scope\n    28\t\n    29\t- Alex's messages win, then the decisions in force, then the governing design documents. Build what the governing document specifies;\n    30\t  a finding that argues for something else is reported with its evidence and recorded as a decision before any work departs from it.\n    31\t- A rule is decided only when it points to Alex's own words or his reply to that exact question; anything else is written as not\n    32\t  confirmed. When his answer replaces layers of a proposal, those layers go. Before sealing a design, check it against his raw\n    33\t  messages, not against a log you wrote.\n    34\t- Do what was asked, in the modules Alex has taken up. A defect in that work, once root-caused, is fixed in the same slice (§1). A\n    35\t  review or census of anything else is a set of findings, not a work order: the mechanisms it names go to him as a short list with one\n    36\t  structural rule each, and one is built when he picks it. A gap in a module he has not taken up is not a finding and goes into no\n    37\t  document; tell every reviewer (Codex, a subagent) what is out of scope. A frozen module (D19, D37) changes only through a new decision.\n    38\t- What goes to Alex: a choice that changes what the system does, as the question, its options and your recommendation; a next step of\n    39\t  work, as one recommendation and one test (§7.3). Settle wording, placement and where a rule is written yourself, and say so in the\n    40\t  report. Never start what only Alex can launch.\n    41\t- **While Alex is not active, the council decides (D439).** A choice or a next step that would go to Alex, including opening a new\n    42\t  version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" (never of the frozen ruler), goes to the council instead:\n    43\t  an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it, round after round, on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals, until\n    44\t  they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, then executed and measured, every trace read by Claude\n    45\t  itself, every round logged with what it taught (Alex, 2026-11-13: \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\"; 2026-11-15, going inactive again (D509): \"我要睡觉了，下来你自行按照我的准则操作，需要深度的审视每一轮run 用council\").\n    46\t  The limits stay: the frozen ruler never changes; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and\n    47\t  provider caps are untouched; paid spending stays within D439's ceiling. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with\n    48\t  both positions, and the cheaper, reversible course is taken.\n    49\t- Add no mechanism, safeguard or substitute rule for a case no one has named. \"No special handling\" keeps the pipeline's shape as it is.\n    91\t## 2. Before writing code: design\n    92\t\n    93\tCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\n    94\tmeans it is not ready:\n    95\t\n    96\t1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\n    97\t   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\n    98\t   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\n    99\t   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   100\t   read and write uses.\n   101\t2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   102\t   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   103\t   against every reader of its output.\n   104\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   105\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n   106\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n   107\t   design and in the question to Alex.\n   108\t\n   109\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\n   110\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\n   111\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\n   112\t  and whether that decision is identity (\"are these the same thing?\") or judgement (\"does this matter?\"); build only the identity part.\n   113\t  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\").\n   114\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\n   115\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\n   116\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\").\n   117\t- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\n   118\t  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\n   119\t  question, not something to build.\n   168\t## 5. Verification\n   169\t\n   170\tVerify at the point the change touches, at the sharpest level that shows it works or fails, and stop there:\n   171\t1. Stored data: reproduce the failing case, show the fix flips it, show a mutant of the fix fails the check ($0).\n   172\t2. Only when what the model is asked changed: re-send just the affected calls.\n   173\t3. The touched suites, plus any standing structural checks the change can affect; the full suite once.\n   174\t4. The gate once, at merge (README, \"Build and check\"). The acceptance once, on the final configuration, scored on the frozen ruler\n   175\t   (§7.1). Never a full rerun per fix.\n   176\t\n   177\t- A further check the change does not need is offered in one line, not run. After the checks that prove a change pass, report and close.\n   178\t- To accept a code change, replay stored decisions through the code deterministically ($0); a sampler run proves nothing about code,\n   179\t  and a cached replay proves nothing about the model.\n   180\t- A re-sent request is the bytes production sends, not the archive's canonical JSON: `model.request_identity` sorts keys for the\n   181\t  archive, `model.call` sends the dict as built. Check a harness by comparing an answer's key order with a production answer's.\n   182\t- Before any paid run, `python3 scripts/preflight.py` replays the stored model answers and matching records of the archives and ledgers\n   183\t  it is given through the current code checks and prompts ($0; it skips rows an earlier run refused, so read what it says it skipped)\n   184\t  and prints, per check, the cases judged and the refusals with reasons (it does not yet replay the coverage-start reading's check:\n   185\t  `CURRENT_STATE.md`, open defects). A changed share or a refusal on a case a person would accept is\n   186\t  diagnosed before the run; a paid run is never the way a check or a prompt is first tried.\n   187\t- An acceptance round is a measurement of the final configuration, not a verification step. A new finding in it is recorded with its\n   188\t  census, not answered with another round.\n   189\t- The product runs end to end before anything else is built, and every merge is accepted on the product's own path. A gate passes only\n   190\t  what it runs: name the check that runs a new path, or say that none does.\n   191\t- Measure before claiming. Label estimates as estimates, report every sample, and treat a number in a design document as a measurement\n   192\t  with a script behind it.\n   323\t- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n   324\t  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n   325\t\n   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md; rg --files | rg 'paid|cost|attain|r22|mutants'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md; rg --files | rg 'paid|cost|attain|r22|mutants'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The paid whole-window comparison of poc-v120 against fresh controls: design, version 1 (D699, D705; for council review)\n     2\t\n     3\t## 0. What it decides, and what it can reach\n     4\t\n     5\tIt decides whether linking (poc-v120: Jev's link questions, version 2; judging-v8's fuller dependency block) makes the linked number\n     6\tquestions' judgements agree with each other over the release window, without harm elsewhere: the evidence for Alex's choice whether\n     7\tthe linking version replaces poc-v118 (D699). It is paired on old-2's trajectory (DESIGN.md §1): every request byte-equal to one old-2\n     8\tsent is answered with old-2's answer; only the readers' judgements are bought.\n     9\t\n    10\t**The attainable verdict ($0, before any send; memory rule \"compute the attainable verdict first\"):** the Data Center question read\n    11\tagainst total revenue for FY2027, on every day both had a conclusion, annual figures taken as the first amount between $200B and $1T in\n    12\teach `implied_outcome` (checked on the known case, old-2 07-12: $410B against $387B):\n    13\t\n    14\t| poc-v118 draw (stored) | days with both | Data Center above total revenue |\n    15\t|---|---|---|\n    16\t| old-1 | 77 | 10 |\n    17\t| old-2 | 72 | 59 (07-12 to 09-14, by up to $59B) |\n    18\t| old-3 | 33 | 2 |\n    19\t\n    20\tThe class exists in every draw and varies widely between draws; old-2's stored path is an extreme and is not a fair control (the July\n    21\tcontrols did not repeat its 07-12 contradiction). A linked sequence that reconciles would show near zero; fresh controls are expected\n    22\tbetween a few and many. The comparison can therefore reach a verdict, and only fresh controls can serve as its baseline.\n    23\t\n    24\t## 1. Arms (paired by draw n = 1, 2, 3)\n    25\t\n    26\t- **linked-n:** poc-v120 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive. Its link jobs are answered only by probe draw n's\n    27\t  answers, matched by request hash (`window_test.probe_answers`; a link job not in it stops the sequence before any purchase), so its\n    28\t  links are exactly probe draw n's proposals, now written. The readers in all three draws: v9 (Data Center FY2027, reads v14), v14\n    29\t  (total revenue FY2027, reads v8), v16 (total CPU FY2027, reads v14), v21 (revenue growth FY2027, reads v16; and v9 in draws 2 and 3).\n    30\t  Their judgements from their link on carry the dependency block, miss the archive and are bought.\n    31\t- **control-n:** poc-v118 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive, with the judge rows of linked-n's readers retired from\n    32\t  each reader's first judgement at or after its link's seq (v9, v14: seq 148; v16: 265; v21: 534), by call id (old-2's call ids rise\n    33\t  with its run, so every later row of that reader, a stored retry included, is retired). Those judgements are fresh samples of the\n    34\t  requests old-2 sent; nothing else is bought.\n    35\t- **old-2's stored path:** a labelled historical baseline, outside the fresh-control figures.\n    36\t- All six sequences run at once (one launcher each, one shared reservation ledger at the ceiling Alex names), so provider drift falls\n    37\t  on both arms alike.\n    38\t\n    39\t## 2. Harness rules (the July harness's, `dependency-design/july_test.py`, extended to the window)\n    40\t\n    41\t- Each sequence: harness-only marker, the store lock, never resumed; a stop is final and makes the comparison inconclusive.\n    42\t- **Allow-list before the budget transport (per sequence, July's latch):** a linked sequence may buy only judge requests of its\n    43\t  readers; a control only judge requests of its retired readers; a link job may only be answered from the probe draw. Any other\n    44\t  request that misses the archive stops the sequence (a cascade the design says cannot happen).\n    45\t- Settlement at published rates with cache writes at 1.25x (`july_test.settled_llm_cost`); reservation from request size (D696).\n    46\t\n    47\t## 3. The $0 proofs before the send\n    48\t\n    49\t1. `v120-replay` (done or running): poc-v120 with each probe draw's own answers meets every probe job and ends equal to old-2.\n    50\t2. Linked dry run per draw, a fake judge answering the readers with markers: the committed links equal probe draw n's proposals; no\n    51\t   link job outside the probe; no circle correction; every non-reader judgement equal to old-2's by question and day; each reader's\n    52\t   first fresh judgement at its link; each reader request shows that day's accepted conclusion of the question it reads (July's chain\n    53\t   check); days added by propagation listed.\n    54\t3. Control dry run per draw: only the retired readers reach the transport, from the right seq; every other judgement equal to old-2's.\n    55\t4. The stop paths and the latch race (July's), on the window.\n    56\t5. Price from old-2's stored judgement tokens for the readers' days, plus the propagation days of the dry run, at published rates.\n    57\t\n    58\t## 4. Reading rule (to be frozen before the send)\n    59\t\n    60\t**Primary line, P (the class this version was built for):** per sequence, the days on which Data Center's annual figure exceeds total\n    61\trevenue's in the same sequence (each question's last conclusion on that day; parser above, its output on every flagged linked day and on\n    62\ta random ten flagged control days checked by hand before counting).\n    63\t- **Pass:** every linked sequence has fewer such days than every control (3 against 3; under no effect this ordering has a chance of\n    64\t  1 in 20), and the controls show at least 2 days each (else \"not tested\").\n    65\t- **Fail:** any linked sequence has as many days as some control, with the harm lines clean: the version does not remove the class.\n    66\t- **Inconclusive:** a stop, a refused reservation, or a control under 2 days.\n    67\t\n    68\t**Harm lines, H (each must hold for a pass):**\n    69\t- H1: no failed article and no stop in the linked arm; first-attempt refusals in the linked arm at most the controls' plus 2.\n    70\t- H2: every judgement outside the readers equal to old-2's by question and day (code).\n    71\t- H3: no grounding error: a reader calling the read question's forecast a market figure, consensus or evidence (code search on\n    72\t  \"consensus\", \"market expect\", \"the market\" within the reference and reasons of reader answers, every hit read by hand).\n    73\t- H4 (the CPU link, round 20): the total does not add the stand-alone CPU forecast on top of a company estimate that already holds it:\n    74\t  every v14 answer whose reasons cite v8, in all three linked sequences, read by hand; a double count is a harm.\n    75\t\n    76\t**Reported beside, not gating:** self-made references on the readers (`reference_census.py`'s measures), linked against controls;\n    77\tJuly's arithmetic-and-assumption reading (rule B) on v9 at seven fixed dates (07-12, 07-26, 08-09, 08-23, 09-06, 09-13, 09-20) in all\n    78\tsix sequences, by Claude and a blind reader; v14 linked against its control (does the total move with the CPU link); v21's implied total\n    79\tagainst v9 and v14; linked-only judgement days.\n    80\t\n    81\t## 5. Cost (estimate; the ceiling is Alex's)\n    82\t\n    83\tOld-2's stored judgements of the readers from their links, at published rates: v9 $0.30, v14 $0.28, v16 $0.15, v21 $0.13, about $0.86 a\n    84\tsequence; linked sequences add the days a changed read question queues its reader (estimated +50%) and about 10% for the dependency\n    85\tblock: about $1.4 a linked sequence; three linked and three controls about $6.8, plus live reservations (at most a few judge calls per\n    86\tsequence at once). To be priced from the dry runs before the ceiling question.\n    87\t\n    88\t## 6. Open points for the council (Claude's, before the review)\n    89\t\n    90\t- **Concurrency inside a sequence.** July's latch held admission and the inner call under one lock, so a sequence's paid calls ran one\n    91\t  at a time. Over the window a linked sequence buys about 300–400 judgements; one at a time (about 30 s each) is about 3 hours per\n    92\t  sequence. Proposal: admission under the lock, the inner call outside it (a day's readers judged together, at most four at once); the\n    93\t  first refusal still closes the latch for every later admission; a call already admitted finishes and settles.\n    94\t- **The primary rule's power.** Old-2's 59 days against old-1's 10 and old-3's 2 show the control count can be small; \"every linked\n    95\t  sequence below every control\" fails if one control lands at 0–1 (then \"not tested\"). The alternative, linked total at most half the\n    96\t  control total, needs the control-against-control check round 13 asked for; with three controls that check is weak either way.\n    97\t- **The parser** reads only the first amount between $200B and $1T; an answer that states its range low-to-high counts its low end.\n    98\t  Every flagged linked day and ten flagged control days are read by hand before counting.\nmutants.log\ncodex-r22.md\ncodex-r22.stream\nmutants.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/config.py | sed -n '80,111p'; nl -ba ../../../tests/test_links.py | sed -n '368,414p'; nl -ba WORDING-V2.md | sed -n '59,108p'; rg -n 'RETIRED_PROBE|v120_replay|with_wording_v2' window_test.py; nl -ba mutants.log | tail -21; rg -n 'links-v2|whole-window' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/config.py | sed -n '80,111p'; nl -ba ../../../tests/test_links.py | sed -n '368,414p'; nl -ba WORDING-V2.md | sed -n '59,108p'; rg -n 'RETIRED_PROBE|v120_replay|with_wording_v2' window_test.py; nl -ba mutants.log | tail -21; rg -n 'links-v2|whole-window' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -10\"","aggregated_output":"    80\tdef _setting(name, raw):\n    81\t    if not isinstance(raw, dict):\n    82\t        raise ConfigError(f'setting {name} is missing')\n    83\t    missing = [key for key in REQUIRED if key not in raw]\n    84\t    if missing:\n    85\t        raise ConfigError(f'setting {name} lacks {missing}')\n    86\t    engine = str(raw.get('engine', 'llm'))\n    87\t    if engine not in ENGINES:\n    88\t        raise ConfigError(f'setting {name}: engine {engine!r} is not one of {ENGINES}')\n    89\t    link_questions = ''\n    90\t    if 'link_questions' in raw:              # named: only in matching, only under jev-links, only one of the exact version strings\n    91\t        if name != 'matching' or engine != 'jev-links':\n    92\t            raise ConfigError(f'setting {name}: link_questions is read only by matching under the engine jev-links')\n    93\t        link_questions = raw['link_questions']\n    94\t        if not isinstance(link_questions, str) or link_questions not in LINK_QUESTIONS:\n    95\t            raise ConfigError(f'setting {name}: link_questions {link_questions!r} is not one of {LINK_QUESTIONS}')\n    96\t    elif name == 'matching' and engine == 'jev-links':\n    97\t        link_questions = 'links-v1'          # unnamed: the first version (poc-v119)\n    98\t    return Setting(name=name, model=str(raw['model']), prompt_version=str(raw['prompt_version']),\n    99\t                   reasoning_effort=str(raw['reasoning_effort']),\n   100\t                   max_output_tokens=int(raw['max_output_tokens']), engine=engine, link_questions=link_questions)\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\tdef load(path):\n   104\t    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   105\t        text = handle.read()\n   106\t    raw = json.loads(text)\n   107\t    for key in ('version', 'provider', 'search_top_n', 'extraction', 'matching', 'rejudging', 'final_verdict'):\n   108\t        if key not in raw:\n   109\t            raise ConfigError(f'config lacks {key}')\n   110\t    canonical = json.dumps({k: v for k, v in raw.items() if not k.startswith('_')}, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   111\t    checksum = hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()[:16]\n   368\t            scripts_replay().refuse_links_engine(version)\n   369\t    scripts_replay().refuse_links_engine(V118)\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\t# ---------- WORDING-V2.md §5 (D705): the link question version ----------\n   373\t\n   374\tdef test_the_question_version_is_read_from_the_matching_setting_and_refused_when_unknown(tmp_path):\n   375\t    assert (V119.matching.link_questions, V120.matching.link_questions, V118.matching.link_questions) == ('links-v1', 'links-v2', '')\n   376\t    assert config.LINK_QUESTIONS == tuple(links.QUESTION_SETS)\n   377\t    raw = json.load(open(os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v120.json')))\n   378\t    refused = {'an unknown version': dict(raw, matching=dict(raw['matching'], link_questions='links-v9')),\n   379\t               'the field under the jev engine': dict(raw, matching=dict(raw['matching'], engine='jev')),\n   380\t               'null under the jev engine': dict(raw, matching=dict(raw['matching'], engine='jev', link_questions=None)),\n   381\t               'null under jev-links (never a silent first version)': dict(raw, matching=dict(raw['matching'], link_questions=None)),\n   382\t               'the field in another setting': dict(raw, rejudging=dict(raw['rejudging'], engine='jev-links', link_questions='links-v2'))}\n   383\t    for index, (case, broken) in enumerate(refused.items()):\n   384\t        path = tmp_path / f'refused-{index}.json'\n   385\t        path.write_text(json.dumps(broken))\n   386\t        with pytest.raises(config.ConfigError):\n   387\t            config.load(str(path))\n   388\t            pytest.fail(f'accepted: {case}')\n   389\t\n   390\t\n   391\tdef test_version_two_asks_its_own_criteria_at_every_stage_and_version_one_keeps_its_own(tmp_path):\n   392\t    for cfg, (reads, sign) in ((dataclasses.replace(V120, collision=None), (links.READS_V2, links.SIGN_V2)), (CFG, (links.READS, links.SIGN))):\n   393\t        folder = tmp_path / cfg.version\n   394\t        folder.mkdir()\n   395\t        conn = two_totals(folder)\n   396\t        stored_link(conn, 'v2', 'v1')                                     # as the circle test: a first answer, a correction, no link\n   397\t        first = recording({'reads__v1': (links.THESIS_READS, 0.8), 'reads__v2': (links.CANDIDATE_READS, 0.8),\n   398\t                           'sign__v1': (links.TOGETHER, 0.8), 'sign__v2': (links.TOGETHER, 0.8)})\n   399\t        correction = scripted({'reads__v1': (links.NEITHER, 0.9), 'reads__v2': (links.NEITHER, 0.9)})\n   400\t\n   401\t        def transport(request):\n   402\t            if any('read itself' in q['instructions'] for q in request['questions'].values()):\n   403\t                first.sent.append(request)\n   404\t                return correction(request)\n   405\t            return first(request)\n   406\t        links.choose(model.Archive(str(folder / 'a.sqlite')), cfg, conn, handover_of(candidate('c1', question='Data Center revenue FY2027?')),\n   407\t                     checked_new('c1'), matching.Lists({'c1': ['v1', 'v2']}, {}), [], transport=transport)\n   408\t        asked = [(qid, q) for request in first.sent for qid, q in request['questions'].items()]\n   409\t        assert {qid.split('__')[0] for qid, _ in asked} == {'reads', 'sign'} and any('read itself' in q['instructions'] for _, q in asked)\n   410\t        for qid, q in asked:\n   411\t            expected = reads if qid.startswith('reads__') else sign\n   412\t            assert q['criteria'] == {k: v for k, v in expected.items() if k in q['criteria']} and len(q['criteria']) >= 2\n   413\t\n   414\t\n    59\t## 4. The probe\n    60\t\n    61\t`window_test.py probe-v2 <scratch> <draw> <ledger> 0.10`: the census pass with the version-2 texts patched into `links.READS` and\n    62\t`links.SIGN` for the pass; every link job is new (the July answers do not match the new texts), so the seq-148 jobs are bought. Three\n    63\tdraws on D700's ledger (spent $0.0266, $0.0734 left); priced as the census (a draw settles about $0.009 at the ledger's rule; the READS\n    64\trequests grow by about 120 tokens a pair). The completeness check, equality with old-2 and the paid-transport record apply as in the\n    65\tcensus; `draw.json` records the wording.\n    66\t\n    67\t## 5. The product version (D705: version 2 as a separately versioned, reviewed configuration)\n    68\t\n    69\t- **Config:** the matching setting gains `link_questions` (`config.Setting.link_questions`; allowed `links-v1`, `links-v2`), accepted\n    70\t  only with the engine `jev-links` (any other engine naming it is refused) and defaulting to `links-v1` there, so `poc-v119.json` is\n    71\t  unchanged in bytes, checksum and requests. `poc/config/poc-v120.json` = poc-v119 with `\"link_questions\": \"links-v2\"`.\n    72\t- **Code:** `links.py` holds both question sets as literal texts (`READS`, `SIGN` for links-v1; `READS_V2`, `SIGN_V2` for links-v2,\n    73\t  byte-equal to the probe's `window_test.wording_v2()`); `reads_question` and `sign_question` take the version; `choose`, `_signed` and\n    74\t  `_corrected` pass `cfg.matching.link_questions`. Nothing else reads the field.\n    75\t- **Entry points:** unchanged: the ordinary launchers refuse the engine `jev-links` under any question version (D694 §0); poc-v120 runs\n    76\t  only in the measurement harness.\n    77\t\n    78\t| Table | Rows |\n    79\t|---|---|\n    80\t| Value × reader | `Setting.link_questions`: read by `links.choose`, `_signed`, `_corrected` (searched); indirectly by `parallel_day.environment_key`, which serializes the whole configuration, so a manifest written before the field existed no longer matches and the parallel day refuses it (its existing guard; round 21); `model.build_request` and every other step ignore it. The two text sets: read by the two builders only. Config rule (round 21): named only in matching under `jev-links`, as one of the exact strings; a null or another section is refused; unnamed under `jev-links`, `links-v1`. The harness's `probe-v2` entry points are retired (the builders read `QUESTION_SETS`, so the old patch no longer changes a request). |\n    81\t| New path × old checks | poc-v119's link requests byte-equal (the v1 pin `LINK_QUESTIONS_SHA` unchanged; `poc-v119.json` untouched); the v2 texts pinned (`LINK_QUESTIONS_V2_SHA`) and equal to the probe's; poc-v120 over the whole window with the probe's own answers replayed by request hash meets every link job of the probe (READS and SIGN) and ends equal to old-2 (`window_test.py v120-replay`); config refuses an unknown question version and the field on another engine. |\n    82\t| State × event | a run keeps one configuration (as for v118/v119, DESIGN.md §0); a store written under poc-v120 and opened under poc-v119 or poc-v118 is read the same (the written rows do not carry the question version; the selection record carries the config checksum); a configuration changed between days is the defined outcome of D694 §0, not a supported mode. |\n    83\t| Prior decisions | D359 (a configuration naming a version the code does not build is refused), D694 §0 (entry points), D695, D703, D705. |\n6:  python3 window_test.py probe-v2-dry / probe-v2   # RETIRED after D705 (the probe's record stays; see RETIRED_PROBE)\n327:def with_wording_v2(run):\n351:    result = with_wording_v2(lambda: without_links(lambda: replay_window(folder, link_answer)))\n362:RETIRED_PROBE = ('retired after D705: links.py now builds version 2 itself (poc-v120, `matching.link_questions` links-v2) and its '\n414:def v120_replay(scratch, draw):\n444:        sys.exit(0 if v120_replay(scratch, sys.argv[3]) else 1)\n446:        raise SystemExit(RETIRED_PROBE)\n     9\tcontrol  [the sign is ignored in the label]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.10s\n    10\tmutant   [the sign is ignored in the label]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.14s\n    11\tcontrol  [the circle check reads stored links only]: exit 0 2 passed, 31 deselected in 0.16s\n    12\tmutant   [the circle check reads stored links only]: exit 1 CAUGHT 2 failed, 31 deselected in 0.20s\n    13\tcontrol  [a correction keeps the offending direction]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.13s\n    14\tmutant   [a correction keeps the offending direction]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.21s\n    15\tcontrol  [READS ignores the configured version]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.16s\n    16\tmutant   [READS ignores the configured version]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.16s\n    17\tcontrol  [SIGN ignores the configured version]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.15s\n    18\tmutant   [SIGN ignores the configured version]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.18s\n    19\tcontrol  [a correction ignores the configured version]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.16s\n    20\tmutant   [a correction ignores the configured version]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.17s\n    21\tcontrol  [config accepts an unknown or null question version]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.11s\n    22\tmutant   [config accepts an unknown or null question version]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.15s\n    23\tcontrol  [config accepts the field in another setting or engine]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.12s\n    24\tmutant   [config accepts the field in another setting or engine]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.15s\n    25\tcontrol  [config reads a null as the first version]: exit 0 1 passed, 32 deselected in 0.11s\n    26\tmutant   [config reads a null as the first version]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 32 deselected in 0.15s\n    27\tcontrol  [a version-2 text drifts by one word]: exit 0 1 passed, 2 deselected in 0.02s\n    28\tmutant   [a version-2 text drifts by one word]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 2 deselected in 0.06s\n    29\texit 0\n10195:  - the whole-window replay waits until a candidate clears the screen;\n10505:## D699 · 2026-11-21 · Alex continues with A: the whole-window measurement of the linking version, designed with the council at $0 first\n10513:- **Next:** the design (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/`), its $0 proofs, council rounds, then the ceiling question to Alex.\n10515:## D700 · 2026-11-21 · Alex approves a $0.10 ceiling for the census of the link decisions before the whole-window run\n10517:- **The question** (after council R round 13 found the July link's direction close to a coin flip, `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md`\n10523:  council passes its harness. The whole-window run keeps its own ceiling question (D699).\n10527:- **The council** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/`, Codex thread `01a1fcdb…`): round 13 NOT READY (no known positive in\n10543:- **Result** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md`, `census-pairs.md`; $0.0266 settled of Alex's $0.10, D700):\n10569:- **The wording** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md`, harness-only, no product file changed): a tie-break (when\n10585:- **Result** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md`, `probe-v2-pairs.md`; $0.0309 settled, $0.0575 of D700's\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
