{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py | sed -n '45,104p;225,297p;430,474p'; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '69,86p;131,171p;265,293p'; rg -n 'CLASS|unsourced|def ' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py\"","aggregated_output":"    45\t    if 'messages' not in request:\n    46\t        return None\n    47\t    text = request['messages'][-1]['content']\n    48\t    return text.split(' ', 2)[1] if text.startswith('Thesis v') else None\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef is_link_request(request):\n    52\t    questions = request.get('questions') or {}\n    53\t    return bool(questions) and all(qid.startswith(('reads__', 'sign__')) for qid in questions)\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tclass Latch:\n    57\t    \"\"\"One per sequence. Admission and the inner call happen under one lock, so the sequence's paid calls run one at a time: a request\n    58\t    is refused, or is admitted and runs to its end, before the next is looked at. The first refusal closes the latch, and every later\n    59\t    request of the sequence, in any thread, a retry included, is refused before the inner transport.\"\"\"\n    60\t\n    61\t    def __init__(self):\n    62\t        import threading\n    63\t        self.lock, self.reason, self.admitted = threading.Lock(), '', []\n    64\t\n    65\t    def run(self, allowed, refusal, label, call):\n    66\t        with self.lock:\n    67\t            if self.reason:\n    68\t                raise Stop(f'the sequence is stopped ({self.reason}): not sent')\n    69\t            if not allowed:\n    70\t                self.reason = refusal\n    71\t                raise Stop(refusal)\n    72\t            self.admitted.append(label)\n    73\t            return call()\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tclass JudgingScope:\n    77\t    \"\"\"The day's judging: only a v9 or v14 judge request may reach the inner transport.\"\"\"\n    78\t\n    79\t    def __init__(self, inner, latch):\n    80\t        self.inner, self.latch, self.sent = inner, latch, []\n    81\t\n    82\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n    83\t        request = args[-1]\n    84\t        view_id = judged_view(request) if len(args) == 2 else None\n    85\t\n    86\t        def call():\n    87\t            self.sent.append(view_id)\n    88\t            return self.inner(*args)\n    89\t        return self.latch.run(view_id in TARGETS, f'unapproved request in judging (thesis {view_id}): not sent', view_id, call)\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\tclass ItemScope:\n    93\t    \"\"\"One item's transport: only link questions, only at seq 148, only in the linked arm.\"\"\"\n    94\t\n    95\t    def __init__(self, inner, seq, linked, sent, latch, link_seq=LINK_SEQ):\n    96\t        self.inner, self.seq, self.linked, self.sent, self.latch, self.link_seq = inner, seq, linked, sent, latch, link_seq\n    97\t\n    98\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n    99\t        request = args[-1]\n   100\t        link = len(args) == 1 and is_link_request(request)\n   101\t\n   102\t        def call():\n   103\t            self.sent.append(('jev', self.seq, sorted(request['questions'])))\n   104\t            return self.inner(*args)\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\tdef fake_jev(readers):\n   228\t    \"\"\"Link questions: `readers` are the theses answered \"the THESIS reads the CANDIDATE\" (sign together); every other pair neither.\"\"\"\n   229\t    def answer(request):\n   230\t        answers = {}\n   231\t        for qid, question in request['questions'].items():\n   232\t            view_id = qid.split('__', 1)[1]\n   233\t            chosen = (links.THESIS_READS if view_id in readers else links.NEITHER) if qid.startswith('reads__') else links.TOGETHER\n   234\t            others = [k for k in question['criteria'] if k != chosen]\n   235\t            probabilities = {k: round(0.2 / len(others), 4) for k in others}\n   236\t            probabilities[chosen] = round(1 - sum(probabilities.values()), 4)\n   237\t            answers[qid] = {'type': 'choice', 'choice': chosen, 'confidence': probabilities[chosen], 'probabilities': probabilities}\n   238\t        return {'model': request['model'], 'answers': answers, 'usage': {'input_tokens': 100, 'output_tokens': 10}}\n   239\t    return answer\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\tdef dispatcher(judge, jev_answer, counter):\n   243\t    def transport(*args):\n   244\t        counter.append(len(args))\n   245\t        return jev_answer(args[0]) if len(args) == 1 else judge(*args)\n   246\t    return transport\n   247\t\n   248\t\n   249\tdef calls_of(archive_path, top):\n   250\t    \"\"\"The target judge calls a sequence made, in order: {view: [(user text, answer data)]}.\"\"\"\n   251\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{archive_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   252\t    out = {}\n   253\t    for request_json, answer_json in archive.execute(\"select request_json, answer_json from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id > ? order by call_id\", (top,)):\n   254\t        request = json.loads(request_json)\n   255\t        out.setdefault(judged_view(request), []).append((request['messages'][-1]['content'], json.loads(answer_json)))\n   256\t    return out\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\tdef previous_reasons(text):\n   260\t    if '[Previous conclusion] none' in text:\n   261\t        return None\n   262\t    return text.split('[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung ', 1)[1].split('; reasons: ', 1)[1].split('\\n', 1)[0]\n   263\t\n   264\t\n   265\tdef chain_checks(summary, archive_path, prefix_ledger, label):\n   266\t    \"\"\"Each target request carries exactly the previous accepted answer of its own question in this sequence (the first: the prefix's);\n   267\t    in the linked arm each v9 request shows exactly that day's accepted v14 comparison point and forecast.\"\"\"\n   268\t    calls = calls_of(archive_path, summary['archive_top'])\n   269\t    prefix = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{prefix_ledger}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   270\t    stored_v9 = prefix.execute(\"select reasons from judgements where view_id='v9' order by judgement_id desc limit 1\").fetchone()[0]\n   271\t    checks = {}\n   272\t    for view_id in TARGETS:\n   273\t        rows = calls.get(view_id, [])\n   274\t        expected = [None if view_id == 'v14' else stored_v9[:800]] + [answer['reasons'] for _, answer in rows[:-1]]\n   275\t        checks[f'{view_id}: each request carries exactly its previous accepted answer'] = bool(rows) and \\\n   276\t            [previous_reasons(text) for text, _ in rows] == expected\n   277\t    if summary['linked']:\n   278\t        v9_days = [j['day'] for j in summary['judgements'] if j['view_id'] == 'v9']\n   279\t        v14 = {j['day']: (j['reference'], j['implied_outcome']) for j in summary['judgements'] if j['view_id'] == 'v14'}\n   280\t        checks['v9: each request shows that day\\'s accepted v14 comparison point and forecast'] = bool(v9_days) and all(\n   281\t            f'Comparison point stated by that judgement: {v14[day][0]}' in text and f'(our own judgement, not evidence): {v14[day][1]}' in text\n   282\t            for (text, _), day in zip(calls.get('v9', []), v9_days))\n   283\t    return checks\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\tdef latch_race():\n   287\t    \"\"\"Worker A is admitted and its call is held open; worker B (an unapproved v8 request) arrives meanwhile; then worker C (v9). B\n   288\t    must wait for A to finish, then be refused and close the latch; C must be refused; only A reaches the inner transport.\"\"\"\n   289\t    import threading\n   290\t    started, release, inner_calls, outcomes = threading.Event(), threading.Event(), [], {}\n   291\t\n   292\t    def inner(provider, request):\n   293\t        inner_calls.append(judged_view(request))\n   294\t        started.set()\n   295\t        release.wait(5)\n   296\t        return {'ok': True}\n   297\t    scope = JudgingScope(inner, Latch())\n   430\t    print(json.dumps(proof, indent=1))\n   431\t    return all(v for k, v in proof.items() if isinstance(v, bool))\n   432\t\n   433\t\n   434\tCACHE_WRITE_SHARE = 1.25        # gpt-6-luna page and the prompt-caching guide, read 2026-11-21: cache writes $0.125 per 1M tokens, 1.25x input\n   435\tJEV_REQUEST_TOKENS = 64000       # TypeSafe's published default per-request limit (docs.typesafe.ai/models, context length), council R round 11\n   436\t\n   437\t\n   438\tdef settled_llm_cost(response, request):\n   439\t    \"\"\"The charge at the published rates: uncached input, cached input (0.1x) and cache writes (1.25x) are three disjoint parts of the\n   440\t    prompt tokens (the guide: \"input tokens use the uncached-input, cached-input, or cache-write rate\"), plus output; None when the\n   441\t    usage counts are not whole numbers with some input (the call then stays charged at its reservation).\"\"\"\n   442\t    usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   443\t    if not isinstance(usage, dict):\n   444\t        return None\n   445\t    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage.get('prompt_tokens'), usage.get('completion_tokens')\n   446\t    details = usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}\n   447\t    cached = details.get('cached_tokens') or 0 if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   448\t    written = details.get('cache_write_tokens') or 0 if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   449\t    whole = lambda n: isinstance(n, int) and not isinstance(n, bool) and n >= 0\n   450\t    if not all(whole(n) for n in (tokens_in, tokens_out, cached, written)) or tokens_in == 0:\n   451\t        return None\n   452\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   453\t    cached = min(tokens_in, cached)\n   454\t    written = min(tokens_in - cached, written)\n   455\t    plain = tokens_in - cached - written\n   456\t    return (plain * price_in + cached * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + written * price_in * CACHE_WRITE_SHARE + tokens_out * price_out) / 1e6\n   457\t\n   458\t\n   459\tdef budget_module():\n   460\t    \"\"\"The comparison runs' budget transport, with this harness's settlement (cache writes at their published rate) and Jev's\n   461\t    reservation at its published per-request limit for each of its attempts; the module is loaded for this harness alone.\"\"\"\n   462\t    import importlib.util\n   463\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('budget_replay_july', REPO / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n   464\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   465\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n   466\t    module.llm_cost = settled_llm_cost\n   467\t    original_jev_estimate = module.jev_estimate\n   468\t    module.jev_estimate = lambda request: max(original_jev_estimate(request),\n   469\t                                              module.jev.ATTEMPTS * JEV_REQUEST_TOKENS * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6)\n   470\t    return module\n   471\t\n   472\t\n   473\tdef bounds():\n   474\t    \"\"\"Every reservation the budget transport makes is an upper bound of what it then settles, checked on all of old-2's stored calls:\n    69\tdef install_stop_gate(ledger):\n    70\t    \"\"\"Process-wide: every `urllib.request.urlopen` call, a helper's internal retry included, first reads the shared ledger. When it is\n    71\t    stopped, or when a registered launcher's lock is free (that launcher died without removing its entry: the gate then stops the\n    72\t    ledger), the call is refused as HTTP 403 (no component retries a 403) and nothing is sent. An attempt whose read came before a stop\n    73\t    was written may finish; one that reads after it is refused. Returns a function that removes the gate.\"\"\"\n    74\t    original = urllib.request.urlopen\n    75\t\n    76\t    def gated(request, *arguments, **keywords):\n    77\t        state = ledger.stop_if_a_launcher_is_gone()\n    78\t        if state.get('stopped'):\n    79\t            raise urllib.error.HTTPError(getattr(request, 'full_url', str(request)), 403,\n    80\t                                         f\"the shared ledger is stopped ({state.get('stop_reason')}): not sent\", {},\n    81\t                                         io.BytesIO(b'{\"error\": {\"type\": \"shared_ledger_stopped\"}}'))\n    82\t        return original(request, *arguments, **keywords)\n    83\t    urllib.request.urlopen = gated\n    84\t\n    85\t    def remove():\n    86\t        if urllib.request.urlopen is gated:\n   131\t    def reserve(self, amount):\n   132\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   133\t            granted = not (state.get('stopped') or state['overrun'] or state['spent'] + state['reserved'] + amount > state['ceiling'])\n   134\t            if granted:\n   135\t                state['reserved'] += amount\n   136\t                state['attempts'] += 1\n   137\t            else:\n   138\t                state['refused'] += 1\n   139\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   140\t                    state['stopped'] = True\n   141\t                    state['stop_reason'] = 'overrun' if state['overrun'] else f'a reservation of ${amount:.6f} would pass the ${state[\"ceiling\"]:.2f} ceiling'\n   142\t        if not granted:\n   143\t            self._note({'refused': amount})                  # after the stop is saved\n   144\t            return False\n   145\t        _LIVE.depth = getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) + 1\n   146\t        return True\n   147\t\n   148\t    @staticmethod\n   149\t    def estimate(request):\n   150\t        \"\"\"The shared reservation of one language-model attempt (WIRING-DESIGN.md §B): `llm_estimate`.\"\"\"\n   151\t        return llm_estimate(request)\n   152\t\n   153\t    def settle(self, reserved, actual, kind='llm', tokens=None):\n   154\t        \"\"\"Settle one attempt. A missing, non-finite, zero or negative charge settles at the whole reservation: an answered paid\n   155\t        request never costs nothing, and a failed attempt is charged its reservation. `kind` (llm, jev, embeddings) and the reported\n   156\t        `tokens` go to the attempt line only.\"\"\"\n   157\t        _LIVE.depth = max(0, getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) - 1)\n   158\t        if not isinstance(actual, (int, float)) or isinstance(actual, bool) or not math.isfinite(actual) or actual <= 0:\n   159\t            actual = reserved\n   160\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   161\t            state['reserved'] = max(0.0, state['reserved'] - reserved)\n   162\t            state['spent'] += actual\n   163\t            if actual > reserved + 1e-12:\n   164\t                state['overrun'] = True\n   165\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   166\t                    state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, 'overrun'\n   167\t        self._note({'kind': kind, 'reserved': reserved, 'charged': actual, **({'tokens': tokens} if tokens is not None else {})})\n   168\t\n   169\t    def stop_if_a_launcher_is_gone(self):\n   170\t        \"\"\"Under the ledger's lock: a registered launcher whose lock no process holds died without removing its entry; the ledger is\n   171\t        stopped. A relaunch calls this before it takes its own lock, so its new lock never makes a stale entry look alive; the stop gate\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n9:  unsourced: no figure in the request the judge was sent equals the reference's first figure, outside the \"[Previous conclusion\"\n14:both own_value and unsourced mark it.\n30:def first_figure(text):\n39:def same(a, b):\n43:def all_figures(text):\n49:def without_previous_conclusion(user_text):\n54:def shown_material(archive, request_sha256):\n63:def census(draw):\n73:        stats = per_question.setdefault(view_id, {'judged': 0, 'with_previous': 0, 'carried': 0, 'own_value': 0, 'unsourced': 0, 'carried_unsourced': 0, 'first_unsourced': None})\n80:            unsourced = bool(figure) and not any(same(figure, shown) for shown in all_figures(shown_material(archive, request_sha256)))\n83:            stats['unsourced'] += unsourced\n84:            stats['carried_unsourced'] += carried and unsourced\n85:            if unsourced and not stats['first_unsourced']:\n86:                stats['first_unsourced'] = day\n87:            marked.append((view_id, day, carried, own, unsourced))\n92:def main():\n96:    print('estimate); \"unsourced\": its first figure is nowhere in the request the judge was sent, outside the previous conclusion.')\n98:    print('| draw | number questions | judgements with a previous one | carried | own value | unsourced | own value and unsourced | carried and unsourced |')\n112:        print('| question | judged | with previous | carried | own value | unsourced | carried and unsourced | first unsourced day | text |')\n114:        for view_id, s in sorted(per_question.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]['unsourced']):\n115:            print(f'| {view_id} | {s[\"judged\"]} | {s[\"with_previous\"]} | {s[\"carried\"]} | {s[\"own_value\"]} | {s[\"unsourced\"]} | {s[\"carried_unsourced\"]} | {s[\"first_unsourced\"] or \"-\"} | {questions.get(view_id, \"?\")[:80]} |')\n117:        sys.exit('positive control failed: old-2 v9 on 2026-09-15 is not marked as both its own value and unsourced')\n118:    print('\\nPositive control: old-2 v9 on 2026-09-15 is marked \"own value\" and \"unsourced\".')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,70p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '65,103p;185,215p;269,358p'; rg -n 'def run|round_of_judgements|close_due|day_runner|changed_views|judging\\\\.' ../../../src/hivemind/replay.py ../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py; rg -n 'def .*close|current_state\\\\(|judgements' ../../../src/hivemind/views/closing.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,70p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '65,103p;185,215p;269,358p'; rg -n 'def run|round_of_judgements|close_due|day_runner|changed_views|judging\\\\.' ../../../src/hivemind/replay.py ../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py; rg -n 'def .*close|current_state\\\\(|judgements' ../../../src/hivemind/views/closing.py\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The whole-window measurement of the linking version: design, version 1 (D699; for council review before any send)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose A (D699, \"continue\"): measure poc-v119 over the whole release window (2026-07-01..09-20, 1,884 articles) against poc-v118,\n     4\tthe measurement designed with the council at $0 first; the paid send waits for the council's pass and a ceiling Alex names. He was told\n     5\tthe measurement would answer four questions, in his order:\n     6\t1. over the whole window, do related number questions still contradict each other;\n     7\t2. which questions did the matching step link, and is any link wrong;\n     8\t3. does the self-made market reference (the system's own figure presented as the market's, `self-reference/RESULT.md`) become rarer;\n     9\t4. does any other question get worse.\n    10\t\n    11\t## 1. The shape: old-2 continued with links\n    12\t\n    13\tEvery request the linking version builds byte-equal to a request old-2 sent is answered with old-2's answer (each sequence works on its\n    14\town copy of old-2's archive); only the requests the links change are bought: the link questions (Jev) and the judgements of a question\n    15\tthat reads a linked question. This is the July test's method (`../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md`)\n    16\tover the whole window.\n    17\t\n    18\tWhy this shape and not an independent forward run:\n    19\t- **Question 4 is answered by construction and checked by code.** No other request carries a judgement of another question:\n    20\t  the extraction request shows open questions with their takes lines (`placement.question_lines`, `placement.takes`: key and group\n    21\t  only); Jev's matching state and thesis text show the question, its ladder and its first two pieces of evidence\n    22\t  (`jev_matching.candidate_state`, `thesis_text`, `matching.describe_view`); a judgement shows its own evidence, its own previous\n    23\t  conclusion, the theme block and its dependencies (`judging.build_prompt`). Linking writes only asset-to-asset rows (D695), so a\n    24\t  changed judgement reaches only the questions that read it. The July test confirmed it: three days, 39 bought calls, every other\n    25\t  request answered from the archive. The code check: every judgement of a question outside the reading chains is equal, row for row,\n    26\t  to old-2's.\n    27\t- **The links' effect is not buried in sampling noise.** A fresh run re-samples 1,884 extractions and about 1,600 judgements; the\n    28\t  questions opened and their evidence would differ from old-2's for reasons that have nothing to do with links.\n    29\t- **Cost:** only the readers' judgements and the link questions are bought (section 6), not the ~$9 of a fresh run.\n    30\t\n    31\tWhat this shape cannot show, stated with the result (round 13): it is a comparison **conditional on old-2's questions and evidence**;\n    32\thow the link step behaves on question sets another draw would open (only old-2's openings are asked); a fresh run's cost and timing;\n    33\tthe idea routes (they read judged positions and reasons, `idea.py`, and the daily replay does not call them: outside this measurement).\n    34\tThe equality check compares nine projections (`rebuild_control.compare`), and unrelated judgements are compared by question and day,\n    35\tsince extra reader judgements shift row ids. The archive matches a request by its canonical identity (sorted keys), as production's\n    36\tarchive does.\n    37\t\n    38\t## 2. The $0 proof that nothing else changes: the `neither` pass\n    39\t\n    40\t`window_test.py neither`: poc-v119 from an empty ledger over the whole window, every link question answered \"neither\" by a fake Jev,\n    41\tevery other request from old-2's archive, anything else stops the pass. An answer old-2's own run refused (the archive keeps it under a\n    42\t`:refused:` suffix, four judge answers) is given back once, so the code refuses it again and the stored retry follows; without that,\n    43\tthe first pass stopped at 07-13 (v7, whose 07-13 judgement was a retry). The pass must end equal to old-2's finished store on views,\n    44\tkeys, rungs, evidence, links, judgements, switches, successions and dependencies (`rebuild_control.compare`), and it lists every\n    45\topening with the pairs shown and which are eligible under D695.\n    46\t\n    47\tResult (`neither.log`, `neither-census.json`; 375 seconds): **equal to old-2 in every table** (43 questions, 5,102 evidence items,\n    48\t6,306 evidence links, 1,616 judgements, 137 rungs, 44 switches, 2 successions, 0 dependencies; last completed seq 1884 in both); the\n    49\tfour refusals met again and none left unmet. The version asks link questions at **14 openings** (every new number question from v2 at\n    50\tseq 8 to v36 at seq 1262), **105 eligible pairs** in 14 jobs: each new number question against every earlier open number question of\n    51\tthe company (1, 2, ... 14 pairs; themes and yes/no questions are not eligible, D695). Openings with pairs:\n    52\t\n    53\t| seq | new question | pairs |\n    54\t|---|---|---|\n    55\t| 8 | v2 commitments for customer and cloud-provider guarantees, FY2027 | 1 |\n    56\t| 49 | v8 stand-alone CPU revenue FY2027 | 2 |\n    57\t| 62 | v9 Data Center revenue FY2027 | 3 |\n    58\t| 148 | v14 total revenue FY2027 | 4 |\n    59\t| 206 | v15 supply commitments, FY2027 report | 5 |\n    60\t| 265 | v16 total CPU revenue FY2027 | 6 |\n    61\t| 321 | v17 total revenue growth FY2028 | 7 |\n    62\t| 534 | v21 total revenue growth FY2027 | 8 |\n    63\t| 746 | v28 gross margin FY2027 | 9 |\n    64\t| 821 | v29 equity investment commitments, FY2027 report | 10 |\n    65\t| 1029 | v32 Poolside licence payment commitment | 11 |\n    66\t| 1102 | v33 gross margin FY2028 | 12 |\n    67\t| 1238 | v35 total revenue FY2028 | 13 |\n    68\t| 1262 | v36 MediaTek convertible-bond investment | 14 |\n    69\t\n    70\t## 3. Before any judgement is bought: the link decisions over the window\n    65\t                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n    66\t            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\n    67\t        },\n    68\t    }\n    69\t    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n    70\t    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n    71\t                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n    72\t    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\n    73\t    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\n    74\t    return schema\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\n    78\t    \"\"\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\n    79\t    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\"\"\"\n    80\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n    81\t        return []\n    82\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n    83\t    out = []\n    84\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select view_id from views where object_kind='theme' order by view_id\"):\n    85\t        theme_id = row['view_id']\n    86\t        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\n    87\t        if not state or not store.is_open(conn, theme_id):\n    88\t            continue\n    89\t        updated = bool(last) and bool(conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and changed=1 and judgement_id>? limit 1',\n    90\t                                                   (theme_id, last['judgement_id'])).fetchone())\n    91\t        rung = store.rungs_of(conn, theme_id)[state['rung'] - 1]\n    92\t        out.append({'view_id': theme_id, 'view': store.view(conn, theme_id), 'state': state, 'rung_label': rung['label'], 'updated': updated})\n    93\t    return out\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\tSTANCE_FIELDS = ['reference', 'implied_outcome']   # D260: what the market expects, and the figure or date the evidence implies\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\tclass JudgementRefused(Exception):\n   100\t    pass\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\tdef topological(conn, view_ids):\n   185\t\n   186\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   187\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   188\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   189\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   190\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n   191\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n   192\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   193\t    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes_in_force(conn, view_id), hidden=hidden,\n   194\t                           full_dependencies=prompt_version in FULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK)\n   195\t    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   196\t        return handle.read(), '\\n'.join(lines)\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\tdef retry_note(errors):\n   200\t    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\tdef themes_shown_in(request_text):\n   204\t    \"\"\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\"\"\"\n   205\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\n   206\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\tdef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n   210\t    \"\"\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\"\"\"\n   211\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n   212\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\tdef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None):\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\tdef upstream(conn, view_id):\n   272\t    \"\"\"Every view this one depends on, directly or through its dependencies.\"\"\"\n   273\t    seen, stack = set(), [view_id]\n   274\t    while stack:\n   275\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, stack.pop()):\n   276\t            target = dep['resolved_to']\n   277\t            if target and target not in seen:\n   278\t                seen.add(target)\n   279\t                stack.append(target)\n   280\t    return seen\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\tdef open_asset_views(conn):\n   284\t    return [v for v in store.open_views(conn) if store.view(conn, v)['object_kind'] != 'theme']\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\tdef queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   288\t    \"\"\"What a changed conclusion of this view queues: its dependants and, for a theme thesis, every open asset thesis. The one rule,\n   289\t    read for a live judgement and for the judgements a resumed round finds committed.\"\"\"\n   290\t    queued = store.dependants_of(conn, view_id)\n   291\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n   292\t        queued = queued + open_asset_views(conn)\n   293\t    return queued\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\tdef queued_by_ledger(conn, seq):\n   297\t    \"\"\"What the judgements already committed at this sequence number queued; a fresh round finds nothing here, a resumed round\n   298\t    finds what the interrupted one had queued in memory.\"\"\"\n   299\t    queued = []\n   300\t    for row in conn.execute('select view_id from judgements where seq=? and changed=1 order by judgement_id', (seq,)):\n   301\t        queued.extend(queued_by_change(conn, row['view_id']))\n   302\t    return queued\n   303\t\n   304\t\n   305\tdef round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):\n   306\t    \"\"\"Judge the open views in changed_views, dependencies first; a changed conclusion queues open dependants.\n   307\t\n   308\t    Views that do not depend on each other are judged at the same time: each level of the dependency order is sent\n   309\t    to the model concurrently (the prompts are built and the answers checked and written in this thread, so the\n   310\t    database connection never crosses threads). A view waits while anything upstream of it is still pending, so a\n   311\t    dependant always reads this round's conclusion of its dependency. A view with no evidence in force stays\n   312\t    unjudged (D59), and a view already judged at this sequence number (a resumed round) is not judged twice.\n   313\t\n   314\t    Among the views ready to be judged, theme theses go first, so an asset thesis reads this round's theme conclusions; a theme judgement that says changed queues every open asset thesis with\n   315\t    evidence in force. The starting queue adds what the ledger says earlier commits at this sequence number queued.\"\"\"\n   316\t    import concurrent.futures\n   317\t\n   318\t    version = cfg.rejudging.prompt_version\n   319\t    schema = schema_for(version)\n   320\t\n   321\t    def eligible(view_id):\n   322\t        return store.is_open(conn, view_id) and not store.has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq) and bool(store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id))\n   323\t\n   324\t    def is_theme(view_id):\n   325\t        return store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme'\n   326\t\n   327\t    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\n   328\t    done, results = set(), []\n   329\t    while pending:\n   330\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n   331\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n   332\t        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   333\t\n   334\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   335\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   336\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   337\t\n   338\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   339\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   340\t        for view_id in level:\n   341\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   342\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   343\t            if errors:\n   344\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   345\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   346\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   347\t                if errors:\n   348\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   349\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   350\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   351\t            done.add(view_id)\n   352\t            results.append(result)\n   353\t            if result['changed']:\n   354\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   355\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\n   356\t                        pending.append(dependant)\n   357\t        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\n   358\t    return results\n../../../src/hivemind/replay.py:51:def run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n../../../src/hivemind/replay.py:52:        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n../../../src/hivemind/replay.py:94:        results = (day_runner(conn, archive, cfg, universe, to_run, day=day, transport=transport, log=log) if day_runner else\n../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py:64:def changed_views_of_day(conn, day):\n../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py:78:    changed = changed_views_of_day(conn, day)\n../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py:83:        judged = judging.round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, sorted(changed), seq, marker, transport=transport)\n../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py:90:    except judging.JudgementRefused as error:\n../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py:97:def run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, *, resume_from=None, transport=None, log=print, extractor=None, matching_workers=1):\n../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py:175:    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'written', 'ok', json.dumps({'changed': sorted(written.changed_views), 'new': written.new_views, 'notes': written.notes[:20]}, ensure_ascii=False))\nrg: ../../../src/hivemind/views/closing.py: IO error for operation on ../../../src/hivemind/views/closing.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The v120 loader now rejects the three configurations that slipped through last round. In the paid design, the proposed scoring can miss contradictions, and the dry proof assumes the upstream question always has a same-day judgement. I’ll check those assumptions against the stored days and requests."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,120p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '60,96p;151,187p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '17,53p'; rg -n 'def close_due|def close|current_state\\\\(' ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py; rg -n 'theme|kind|chosen_parent|narrowest_links' ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,120p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '60,96p;151,187p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '17,53p'; rg -n 'def close_due|def close|current_state\\\\(' ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py; rg -n 'theme|kind|chosen_parent|narrowest_links' ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"    51\tdef run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n    52\t        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n    53\t    items_db = testdb.open_db(testdb_path)\n    54\t    conn = store.open_db(views_path)\n    55\t    refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn)\n    56\t    last_done = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    57\t    start = from_day\n    58\t    if last_done and from_day <= last_done:\n    59\t        next_day = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(last_done) + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()\n    60\t        if next_day > until_day:\n    61\t            raise BackdatingError(f'views database already completed {last_done}; nothing to run before it')\n    62\t        log(f'resuming after the last completed day {last_done}')\n    63\t        start = next_day\n    64\t    last_written = conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0').fetchone()[0]\n    65\t    if last_written and start < last_written:\n    66\t        raise BackdatingError(f'views database already holds rounds of {last_written}; a replay cannot start before it (D31)')\n    67\t    totals = {'items': 0, 'extracted': 0, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 0, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0,\n    68\t              'evidence': 0, 'new_views': 0, 'judged': 0, 'changed': 0, 'closed': 0}\n    69\t    calls_before, cost_before, *_ = archive.totals()\n    70\t    for day in calendar_days(start, until_day):\n    71\t        day_stats = {k: 0 for k in totals}\n    72\t        day_cost_before = archive.totals()[1]\n    73\t        processed = 0\n    74\t        to_run = []\n    75\t        for item in testdb.feed(items_db, day, day):\n    76\t            if item['publication_day'] > day:\n    77\t                raise LookAheadError(f'{item[\"input_id\"]} is dated {item[\"publication_day\"]}, after replay day {day}')\n    78\t            if only_objects and not any(o['value'] in only_objects for o in item['object_identifiers']):\n    79\t                continue\n    80\t            if max_items_per_day and processed >= max_items_per_day:\n    81\t                break\n    82\t            day_stats['items'] += 1\n    83\t            route = dispatch.route(conn, item, universe)\n    84\t            if route.kind != 'extract':\n    85\t                day_stats[route.kind] += 1\n    86\t                if route.kind == 'skipped':\n    87\t                    processed += 1      # written by an earlier run of this day: a restart keeps the day's item limit\n    88\t                if route.kind == 'merged':\n    89\t                    dispatch.mark(conn, item, 0, 'merged', 'ok', route.reason)\n    90\t                    conn.commit()\n    91\t                continue\n    92\t            processed += 1\n    93\t            to_run.append((item, route))\n    94\t        results = (day_runner(conn, archive, cfg, universe, to_run, day=day, transport=transport, log=log) if day_runner else\n    95\t                   (round_module.run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, route.sequence_no, resume_from=route.resume_from, transport=transport, log=log)\n    96\t                    for item, route in to_run))\n    97\t        finished = 0\n    98\t        try:\n    99\t            for index, result in enumerate(results):\n   100\t                if index >= len(to_run) or result.input_id != to_run[index][0]['input_id']:\n   101\t                    raise RuntimeError('day runner returned results out of input order')\n   102\t                finished += 1\n   103\t                day_stats['extracted'] += 1\n   104\t                day_stats['evidence'] += result.evidence\n   105\t                day_stats['new_views'] += result.new_views\n   106\t                day_stats['judged'] += result.judged\n   107\t                day_stats['changed'] += result.changed\n   108\t                if result.failed:\n   109\t                    day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   110\t                    log(f'  ! {result.input_id[:60]}: {result.failed}')\n   111\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'item failed; day {day} remains resumable: {result.failed}')\n   112\t                if spend_cap_usd is not None and archive.totals()[1] - cost_before > spend_cap_usd:\n   113\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'spend cap {spend_cap_usd} reached on {day}')\n   114\t        finally:\n   115\t            if hasattr(results, 'close'):\n   116\t                results.close()\n   117\t        if finished != len(to_run):\n   118\t            raise RuntimeError('day runner did not complete every routed item')\n   119\t        seq = store.next_sequence(conn) - 1\n   120\t        judged = round_module.judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, transport=transport, log=log)\n    60\t    _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_refused_twice', 'matching refused twice: ' + note, item['category'])\n    61\t    return None\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef changed_views_of_day(conn, day):\n    65\t    \"\"\"The views whose reading changed on a replay day: the union of the 'written' records of that day's items and of the coverage-start reading's\n    66\t    record dated that day (D364: the questions it linked starting figures to are judged in the first day's round).\"\"\"\n    67\t    changed = set()\n    68\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select reason from processing_steps where step in ('written', 'baseline') and result='ok' and publication_day=?\", (day,)):\n    69\t        changed.update(json.loads(row['reason']).get('changed', []))\n    70\t    return changed\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, *, transport=None, log=print):\n    74\t    \"\"\"D63: one re-judging round per day over every open view whose reading changed that day, dependencies first,\n    75\t    recorded under the day's own processing record (input 'day:<date>'); a view already judged at this sequence\n    76\t    number (a resumed day) is not judged twice.\"\"\"\n    77\t    marker = {'input_id': f'day:{day}', 'publication_day': day}\n    78\t    changed = changed_views_of_day(conn, day)\n    79\t    result = RoundResult(marker['input_id'])\n    80\t    if not changed:\n    81\t        return result\n    82\t    try:\n    83\t        judged = judging.round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, sorted(changed), seq, marker, transport=transport)\n    84\t        result.judged = len(judged)\n    85\t        result.changed = sum(1 for j in judged if j['changed'])\n    86\t        result.cost += sum(j['cost'] for j in judged)\n    87\t        result.cached_calls += sum(1 for j in judged if j['cached'])\n    88\t        dispatch.mark(conn, marker, seq, 'judged', 'ok', f'{len(changed)} views changed, {len(judged)} judged, {result.changed} changed conclusions')\n    89\t        conn.commit()\n    90\t    except judging.JudgementRefused as error:\n    91\t        return _fail(conn, marker, seq, result, 'judged', 'judgement_refused_twice', 'judgement refused twice: ' + str(error), 'day')\n    92\t    except Exception as error:\n    93\t        return _fail(conn, marker, seq, result, 'judged', 'judging_failed', 'judging: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n    94\t    return result\n    95\t\n    96\t\n   151\t            return result\n   152\t        second_pass = checked2.evidence\n   153\t    # D694, D695: under the engine jev-links, the reading links between a newly opened number question and the number questions it was\n   154\t    # shown, chosen once matching has settled what opens (views/links.py); recorded per attempt whatever happens next\n   155\t    proposed, attempt = None, None\n   156\t    if cfg.matching.engine == links.ENGINE:\n   157\t        attempt = links.attempt_id(conn, item)\n   158\t        try:\n   159\t            proposed, chosen = links.choose(archive, cfg, conn, handover, checked, lists, shown, transport=transport)\n   160\t        except links.Refused as error:\n   161\t            links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'failed', error.record)\n   162\t            return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'linking_refused', 'linking: ' + str(error), 'linking')\n   163\t        links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'proposed', chosen)\n   164\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   165\t    # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   166\t    try:\n   167\t        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass, proposed_links=proposed)\n   168\t    except Exception as error:\n   169\t        if attempt:\n   170\t            links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'failed', {'error': repr(error)[:300]})\n   171\t        return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'written', 'writing_failed', 'writing: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   172\t    if attempt:\n   173\t        links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'committed', {'links': written.links})\n   174\t    result.new_views = len(set(written.new_views.values()))\n   175\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'written', 'ok', json.dumps({'changed': sorted(written.changed_views), 'new': written.new_views, 'notes': written.notes[:20]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   176\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', '')\n   177\t    conn.commit()\n   178\t    return result\n    17\tThe reference (D260): the rung is the forecast the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects\n    18\t(consensus, guidance, the stated plan); the answer states the reference and the outcome the evidence implies, both stored beside the\n    19\trung, and an empty one is refused.\"\"\"\n    20\timport dataclasses\n    21\timport json\n    22\timport re\n    23\t\n    24\tfrom .. import config, model, vocabulary\n    25\tfrom . import store\n    26\t\n    27\tPUSHES = vocabulary.PUSHES\n    28\tSUPPORTED_VERSIONS = ('judging-v7', 'judging-v8')   # D354: the frozen judging prompt; D694: v8 = v7's text with the fuller dependency block\n    29\tFULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK = ('judging-v8',)\n    30\tREADINGS = 5                      # a piece is shown in the thesis's first five judgements after it arrives\n    31\tBASIS = 10                        # and while one of the last ten judgements cited it\n    32\tTHEME_REASONS_CHARS = 300\n    33\tUPDATED_MARK = 'updated since this thesis was last judged'\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\tdef require_supported(prompt_version):\n    37\t    \"\"\"Refuses a judging prompt version this code does not build, before any request is made.\"\"\"\n    38\t    if prompt_version not in SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\n    39\t        raise ValueError(f'judging {prompt_version!r} is not built; this code builds only {\", \".join(SUPPORTED_VERSIONS)} (D354)')\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef evidence_in_view(conn, view_id):\n    43\t    \"\"\"(the pieces a judgement of this thesis reads, how many pieces in force are not shown): the arrivals (linked after the\n    44\t    READINGS-th most recent judgement, or all when there are fewer) and the basis (cited by one of the last BASIS judgements),\n    45\t    both among the evidence in force.\"\"\"\n    46\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\n    47\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\n    48\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\n    49\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n    50\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\n    51\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\n    52\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\n    53\t\n201:def close_view(conn, view_id, reason, by_whom, seq):\n234:def current_state(conn, view_id):\n14:    'views': 'view_id text primary key, object_id text, object_kind text, kind text, looks_at text, question text, due_day text, year text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text, created_at text',\n18:    'judgements': 'judgement_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, rung integer, reasons text, cited_evidence_json text, cited_views_json text, pushes_json text, changed integer, why_changed text, config_checksum text, call_id integer, request_sha256 text, publication_day text, theme_pushes_json text, reference text, implied_outcome text',\n25:    'dependencies': 'dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer, kind text default \\'\\'',   # kind: '' (a seed's or the generative matcher's row, read as before) or 'reads' (a chosen reading link, D694)\n31:    'review_pool_entries': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, kind text, key text, example_json text, seq integer',\n83:def create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\n84:    insert(conn, 'views', view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=kind, looks_at=looks_at,\n150:    if 'theme_pushes_json' not in judgement_columns:\n151:        conn.execute('alter table judgements add column theme_pushes_json text')     # D195: judgements written before the theme block read as []\n155:    if 'kind' not in {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(dependencies)')}:\n156:        conn.execute(\"alter table dependencies add column kind text default ''\")   # D694: every row written before reads ''\n259:    reads = \" and coalesce(kind, '') != 'reads'\" if 'kind' in {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(dependencies)')} else ''\n296:    seq (day_start_seq) whose last switch at that seq is open, the objects' own and every theme, in creation order; before the first\n298:    so the list is the same for every item of the day whatever the day's items write. Question, looks_at, kind, object and due day only.\"\"\"\n301:    for v in conn.execute('select view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, created_seq from views where created_seq <= ? order by created_seq', (seq,)):\n302:        if v['kind'] != 'theme' and v['object_id'] not in object_ids:\n310:def views_for_prompt(conn, object_ids, themes=False):\n312:    depends on whom; question, looks_at and due day only. With themes, every open theme thesis follows the objects' own\n313:    (A, extraction v19): a company item's statement about a theme matter links to the theme thesis instead of being dropped.\"\"\"\n320:    if themes:\n321:        for row in conn.execute(\"select view_id from views where kind='theme' order by created_seq\"):\n473:def pool(conn, kind, key, example, seq):\n474:    insert(conn, 'review_pool_entries', kind=kind, key=key, example_json=json.dumps(example, ensure_ascii=False)[:4000], seq=seq)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'old-[123]|attainable|first amount|200B' PAID-DESIGN.md ../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness --glob '*.py' --glob '*.md' | tail -28; ls ../../../poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py | sed -n '1,90p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '29,53p'; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md | sed -n '5,22p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'old-[123]|attainable|first amount|200B' PAID-DESIGN.md ../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness --glob '*.py' --glob '*.md' | tail -28; ls ../../../poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py | sed -n '1,90p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '29,53p'; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md | sed -n '5,22p'\"","aggregated_output":"../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection_census.py:52:    for draw in ('old-1', 'old-2', 'old-3'):\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/JULY-RESULT.md:4:nothing refused or overrun). Six sequences from old-2's state at the end of 07-09, judged fresh 07-10..07-12: three under poc-v118\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round2-brief.md:19:   second outcome is D191 point 2's later addition happening at the moment the whole is created (old-2: total revenue opened at seq\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round2-brief.md:27:4. **Filing, sized on the product.** In old-2, **106** evidence items are linked to both v9 (Data Center) and v14 (total revenue);\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round2-brief.md:35:   own)\". Agree? Any risk that a whole's own self-made reference is passed down as the market's (old-1 v1 is a total-type question with\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round2-brief.md:42:7. **The test.** I accept your window (old-2, just before seq 148 to 07-12, three fresh control and three linked sequences, real\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round3-brief.md:5:   `implied_outcome` as \"the system's forecast for [question]\", both outside the bounded reasons excerpt; no \"market\" label (old-1 v1\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r4.md:19:**5. Rewrite `READS` and `SIGN` around the chosen reader.** For old-2, the expected `READS` answer is `thesis_reads_candidate`. `SIGN` then asks the wrong conditional: it changes Data Center and asks what happens to total revenue, although the chosen reader is Data Center. Ask about the effect of the **read question’s** outcome on the **reading question**. Under a stated continuing-mix assumption, `together` is defensible for July. A bound alone can be loosened without changing the most likely answer, so `no_clear_sign` needs to cover that case. This leaves relevance and sign with the model. Code should check identity, allowed answers and whether the result maps to a label. Specify whether Jev’s returned `choice` or the rounded probabilities decide ties. Two displayed scores can both be `0.50`. [Design question texts and threshold](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:26) · [Jev choice validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:52)\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round10-brief.md:4:1. Reservations bound settlements: `july_test.py bounds` over all of old-2's stored calls (largest settled/reserved 0.30); with each\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round10-brief.md:12:4. `prepare` checks the copy against old-2 (the proved comparison) and its last completed day 07-09 before any transport; preflight run\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md:4:- `selection-census.md`: the matcher's \"part_of\" is undirected by its own criterion and noisy (old-2 seq 148: total revenue FY2027\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md:5:  \"part_of\" Data Center 0.99; old-1 seq 1410: FY2028 growth \"part_of\" FY2027 Data Center 0.79; aggregates \"part_of\" single deals).\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md:8:- Creation order differs: old-1 and old-3 open total revenue first (seq 22); **old-2 opens Data Center at seq 62 and total revenue at\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md:10:- **Filing:** in old-2, **106** evidence items are linked to both v9 (Data Center) and v14 (total). With D265 read literally on a\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md:28:   ends), not guessed. Risk: keys are model-written (`scope_source: model`; old-2 v8 stand-alone CPU has measure `other` and would be\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md:29:   missed; old-3 v14's question says \"total CPU\" while its scope says \"Vera CPU\"). A missed pair costs nothing new; a wrong pair\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:1:\"\"\"$0 step 2 of D694: rebuild old-2's ledger as it stood at the end of 2026-07-09 (the July test's starting state) by replaying the\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:2:product (poc-v118) from 2026-07-01 over old-2's own stored answers. Every request must be answered from the archive: the transport\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:8:Then it compares the rebuilt ledger with old-2's finished store up to the end of 07-09: views, keys, rungs, evidence, links and\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:20:OLD2 = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod'\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:149:- Worked case (old-2 07-10): R = v9 (direction −1, Strongly bullish first: favourable end high), T = v14 (−1), `together` → T's high\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:199:| no-link requests byte-equal | proved at $0: poc-v119 over old-2's 07-01..07-09 with the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport equals the rebuilt v118 prefix (every other request from the archive) |\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:201:| filing with a `reads` row | no link removed: re-file old-2's stored readings after seq 148 with the link present (105 shared statements, `filing-exposure.md`) |\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.md:5:The clearest example is old-2. Data Center opened on July 6, and total revenue opened on July 10. On July 12, the system forecast **$400–410B for Data Center and about $387B for all of NVIDIA**. A rule that chooses links only when the reading question opens cannot connect that pair in the useful direction. The September probe inserted the link directly into a copy of the ledger. It showed that the judge can use the link, but skipped how the product would choose and write it. [Stored selection census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md:59) · [Probe setup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/probe.py:36)\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.md:11:**Open for the council.** Give Jev a directed choice within matching, using the questions already shown by search and extraction and the questions opened by the same item. Have the model decide whether a conclusion is useful, including an explicit choice of no link. Code verifies the endpoints, exact identities, final opening decisions, labels and absence of cycles. The existing `part_of` answer can inform the model. It says “in either direction,” and in old-1 it scored both FY2027 and FY2028 total revenue as related to FY2027 Data Center. The stored measure, scope, period, basis and unit help the model distinguish those cases. They cannot decide whether reading the conclusion will improve the forecast. The final design still needs an exact request and a refusal path that works with Jev. D51 supplies the existing matching setting and the limit on what may be shown. [Jev criteria and candidate loop](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:25) · [Selection census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md:8) · [Ownership table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md:112)\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.md:15:Creation can reach the useful pair in old-1 and old-3. It cannot make the existing Data Center question read the newly opened total in old-2. D191 point 2 already permits a later item to add a link to an existing question. D368 calls for that work to be designed and measured as its own slice. The council still has to specify when that later item may propose the link and how matching records and corrects a conflicting proposal. [Stored selection census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md:59) · [D191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2503) · [D368](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3968)\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.md:41:For an isolated pair, the increase is **zero or one accepted judge call per day**. It is zero if both were already queued, the upstream conclusion did not change, or the reader is ineligible. It is one if the link is the sole reason an eligible reader is queued. Initial binding or moving to a successor can also queue that reader once. Retries and any wider chain are separate. At the published Luna rates of **$0.10/M input, $0.01/M cached input and $0.50/M output**, one extra call the size of old-2’s September 20 Data Center call would cost an estimated **$0.0056** before cache discounts. Existing calls that receive the line also incur its added input tokens. [Rates and usage calculation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:26)\n../../../docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.md:62:**One test.** Use old-2 from just before the July 10 item at sequence 148 through July 12. First rebuild the stored control at $0 and prove that the new path can select and write **existing Data Center reads newly opened total revenue** through real matching and writing. Exercise the refusal, filing, historical-read and resume cases with stored answers or labelled fakes. For the paid comparison, run three fresh control sequences and three linked sequences from the same starting state. Buy only the affected calls. Replay unrelated calls by exact request identity and stop on an unexpected miss. Each sequence must use its own accepted forecasts and citations on the next day. A failed selection counts as a failed sequence. [Stored selection case](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md:59) · [Why the earlier fixed-answer replay cannot substitute](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md:285)\nledgers\nnew-1\nnew-1.launcher.log\nnew-1.pid\nnew-2\nnew-2.launcher.log\nnew-2.pid\nnew-3\nnew-3.launcher.log\nnew-3.pid\nold-1\nold-1.launcher.log\nold-1.pid\nold-2\nold-2.launcher.log\nold-2.pid\nold-3\nold-3.launcher.log\nold-3.pid\n     1\t\"\"\"$0 census of the self-made market reference (D692): in the three finished poc-v118 draws, how often a judgement's `reference`\n     2\t(the field judging-v7 asks for: \"what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or\n     3\tdeadline)\") is the system's own earlier figure rather than a market figure.\n     4\t\n     5\tTwo measures, per judgement of a question that already has a previous judgement:\n     6\t  carried:   the reference says it was taken from the previous judgement or conclusion (the words \"previous\", \"prior\" or \"carried\");\n     7\t  own_value: the reference's first figure equals the first figure of the previous judgement's `implied_outcome` (the system's own\n     8\t             estimate), within 0.5% (the same unit word: billion, trillion, million or percent).\n     9\t  unsourced: no figure in the request the judge was sent equals the reference's first figure, outside the \"[Previous conclusion\"\n    10\t             section (the stored request, found in the draw's archive by the judgement's request_sha256). A figure the evidence\n    11\t             states (a signed amount, a guidance figure, a rung bound) is therefore not counted, whatever the estimate equals.\n    12\tA judgement counts once per measure. The stores are opened read-only. The positive control is old-2 v9 on 2026-09-15 (reference\n    13\t\"$414 billion\", the 09-14 implied outcome \"$414 billion\", not in the evidence shown): the script exits with an error unless\n    14\tboth own_value and unsourced mark it.\n    15\t\n    16\t  python3 reference_census.py > reference-census.md\n    17\t\"\"\"\n    18\timport re\n    19\timport sqlite3\n    20\timport sys\n    21\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    22\t\n    23\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n    24\tRUNS = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    25\tFIGURE = re.compile(r'\\$?\\s?(\\d+(?:,\\d{3})*(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s?(trillion|billion|million|bn|B\\b|T\\b|%|percent)', re.IGNORECASE)\n    26\tUNIT = {'trillion': 1e12, 't': 1e12, 'billion': 1e9, 'bn': 1e9, 'b': 1e9, 'million': 1e6, '%': 1.0, 'percent': 1.0}\n    27\tCARRIED = re.compile(r'\\b(previous|prior|carried)\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef first_figure(text):\n    31\t    match = FIGURE.search(text or '')\n    32\t    if not match:\n    33\t        return None\n    34\t    unit = match.group(2).lower()\n    35\t    kind = 'percent' if unit in ('%', 'percent') else 'amount'\n    36\t    return kind, float(match.group(1).replace(',', '')) * UNIT[unit]\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tdef same(a, b):\n    40\t    return a and b and a[0] == b[0] and abs(a[1] - b[1]) <= 0.005 * max(abs(a[1]), abs(b[1]), 1e-9)\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef all_figures(text):\n    44\t    for match in FIGURE.finditer(text or ''):\n    45\t        unit = match.group(2).lower()\n    46\t        yield ('percent' if unit in ('%', 'percent') else 'amount'), float(match.group(1).replace(',', '')) * UNIT[unit]\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tdef without_previous_conclusion(user_text):\n    50\t    \"\"\"The request's user text with the \"[Previous conclusion\" section removed (it runs to the next bracketed header or the end).\"\"\"\n    51\t    return re.sub(r'\\n\\[Previous conclusion[^\\n]*(?:\\n(?!\\[)[^\\n]*)*', '\\n', user_text)\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef shown_material(archive, request_sha256):\n    55\t    row = archive.execute(\"select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1\", (request_sha256,)).fetchone()\n    56\t    if not row:\n    57\t        raise SystemExit(f'request {request_sha256} not in the archive: the census cannot judge it')\n    58\t    import json\n    59\t    messages = json.loads(row[0])['messages']\n    60\t    return without_previous_conclusion(messages[-1]['content'])\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef census(draw):\n    64\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUNS / draw}/prod/views.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    65\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUNS / draw}/prod/archive.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    66\t    questions = dict(conn.execute('select view_id, question from views'))\n    67\t    units = dict(conn.execute('select view_id, unit from view_keys'))\n    68\t    rows = conn.execute('select view_id, judgement_id, publication_day, reference, implied_outcome, request_sha256 from judgements order by view_id, judgement_id').fetchall()\n    69\t    per_question, marked, previous = {}, [], {}\n    70\t    for view_id, judgement_id, day, reference, implied, request_sha256 in rows:\n    71\t        if units.get(view_id) not in ('USD', 'percent'):\n    72\t            continue\n    73\t        stats = per_question.setdefault(view_id, {'judged': 0, 'with_previous': 0, 'carried': 0, 'own_value': 0, 'unsourced': 0, 'carried_unsourced': 0, 'first_unsourced': None})\n    74\t        stats['judged'] += 1\n    75\t        if view_id in previous:\n    76\t            stats['with_previous'] += 1\n    77\t            carried = bool(CARRIED.search(reference or ''))\n    78\t            figure = first_figure(reference)\n    79\t            own = bool(same(figure, first_figure(previous[view_id])))\n    80\t            unsourced = bool(figure) and not any(same(figure, shown) for shown in all_figures(shown_material(archive, request_sha256)))\n    81\t            stats['carried'] += carried\n    82\t            stats['own_value'] += own\n    83\t            stats['unsourced'] += unsourced\n    84\t            stats['carried_unsourced'] += carried and unsourced\n    85\t            if unsourced and not stats['first_unsourced']:\n    86\t                stats['first_unsourced'] = day\n    87\t            marked.append((view_id, day, carried, own, unsourced))\n    88\t        previous[view_id] = implied\n    89\t    return questions, per_question, marked\n    90\t\n    29\t# gpt-6-astra: \"$10 input … $50 output\" per million tokens; D632's comparison only).\n    30\t# claude-opus-5-5: Anthropic's first-party list price, $4 input and $20 output per million tokens (the claude-api skill's model table,\n    31\t# cached 2026-11-03); Alex's Opus trial only (2026-11-16, \"你试试看opus\"). Cache reads ($0.20) are priced at CACHED_INPUT_SHARE, an over-estimate.\n    32\t# gpt-6-luna: the published standard rates on 2026-10-25 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna: $0.10/M input, $0.50/M output,\n    33\t# cached input $0.01/M). Until this date the table carried (1.25, 10.0), so every cost_usd recorded before it is 12.5x (input) to 20x (output)\n    34\t# the published rate; the token columns are the measurement, the bill is the provider's.\n    35\tPRICES = {'gpt-6-luna': (0.10, 0.50), 'gpt-6.1-sol': (2.00, 10.00), 'gpt-6-astra': (10.00, 50.00), 'claude-opus-5-5': (4.00, 20.00), 'deepseek-flash': (0.30, 1.20), 'deepseek-v4-pro': (1.32, 3.96),\n    36\t          'jev-1.14.0': (0.042, 0.0)}   # Jev: docs.typesafe.ai/models, 2026-10-25; output free   # DeepSeek: peak-hour list prices, cache misses (2026-10-23 pricing page)\n    37\tCACHED_INPUT_SHARE = 0.10          # cached input tokens are priced at 10% of the input rate (gpt-6-luna page, read again 2026-10-27)\n    38\t\n    39\tSCHEMA_SQL = \"\"\"\n    40\tcreate table if not exists model_calls (\n    41\t  call_id integer primary key autoincrement, purpose text, config_version text, config_checksum text, model text,\n    42\t  request_sha256 text unique, request_json text, response_json text, answer_json text, prompt_chars integer,\n    43\t  input_tokens integer, output_tokens integer, cost_usd real, seconds real, created_at text\n    44\t);\n    45\tcreate index if not exists model_calls_sha on model_calls(request_sha256);\n    46\t\"\"\"\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass SchemaError(ValueError):\n    50\t    pass\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tclass TransportError(RuntimeError):\n     5\t## Reading rule (frozen before the send; council R round 2, `codex-r2.md` §7(b), with round 3)\n     6\t- **A. Comparable answers:** both 07-12 answers give a FY2027 forecast in USD for their own quantity (a range by its stated ends);\n     7\t  quarters recorded where both give comparable figures; a missing annual figure leaves reconciliation untested.\n     8\t- **B. Arithmetic and sources:** reported figures keep their amount and scope; the arithmetic follows from the stated inputs within\n     9\t  rounding; each assumption that materially sizes the result is disclosed and supported by the material available that day; a linked\n    10\t  forecast is treated as a forecast with assumptions.\n    11\t- **C. Room for the rest:** the high end of the Data Center forecast is at least $6B below the low end of the company forecast (the Q1\n    12\t  floor: $81.6B total minus $75.25B Data Center); each comparable quarter keeps the segment within the total.\n    13\t- **D. The link did the work (linked arm):** matching chose \"v9 reads v14\", the writer committed it at seq 148, and v9 used v14's\n    14\t  forecast in its calculation or as a stated bound; delivery and use of the Bloomberg-compiled $393B (e195) recorded separately; a\n    15\t  mention or citation alone earns no credit.\n    16\t- **Pass:** at least two of three linked sequences meet A–D; at most one control meets A–C; no first-attempt refusal added and no new\n    17\t  material grounding error on either question across 07-10..07-12 (relabelling a system forecast as a market estimate, or treating\n    18\t  $393B as a Data Center consensus, is one). **Inconclusive:** two or more controls reconcile, fewer than two comparable sequences in\n    19\t  either arm, or a ceiling stop. **Fail:** a new material error, an added refusal, fewer than two correct link selections, or any other\n    20\t  miss. Failures take precedence.\n    21\t- **Readers:** Claude's marks written first, then a fresh blind Codex reader on the six sequences under shuffled labels, the key outside\n    22\t  the repository; every sequence reported.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections as co, json, math, pathlib, re, sqlite3, statistics\nimport window_test as w\nfrom hivemind import config, model\nroot=w.REPO\ndef sql(path): return sqlite3.connect(path.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nv=sql(w.OLD2/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\na=sql(w.OLD2/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'')\nstarts={'\\\\''v9'\\\\'':148,'\\\\''v14'\\\\'':148,'\\\\''v16'\\\\'':265,'\\\\''v21'\\\\'':534}\npr=w.july_test.budget_module()\nrefused=[]\nattempts={k:[] for k in starts}\ndates={k:{} for k in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'',*starts)}\ncases=co.defaultdict(dict)\nfor view,seq,d,change,call,sha,out in v.execute('\\\\''select view_id, seq, publication_day, changed, call_id, request_sha256, implied_outcome from judgements order by judgement_id'\\\\''):\n if view not in dates: continue\n dates[view][d]=bool(change)\n if view in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'') and d>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'': cases[d][view]=out\n if view in starts and seq>=starts[view]:\n    r=a.execute('\\\\''select call_id, request_json,response_json,seconds from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call,)).fetchone()\n    assert a.execute('\\\\''select request_sha256 from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call,)).fetchone()[0]==sha\n    attempts[view].append((d,*r))\nfor c,sha,req,res,sec in a.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_sha256,request_json,response_json,seconds from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\'' and (request_sha256 like '\\\\''%:refused:%'\\\\'' or request_sha256 like '\\\\''%:schema:%'\\\\'')\\\"):\n rr=json.loads(req)\n refused.append((c,w.july_test.judged_view(rr),sha,pr.llm_cost(json.loads(res),rr)))\ntotal=0; reserve=[]; seconds=[]\nfor k,ls in attempts.items():\n cost=sum(pr.llm_cost(json.loads(res),json.loads(req)) for d,c,req,res,sec in ls)\n total+=cost\n reserve.extend(pr.llm_estimate(json.loads(req)) for d,c,req,res,sec in ls)\n seconds.extend(sec for d,c,req,res,sec in ls)\n print(k,len(ls),'\\\\''first seq/day/call'\\\\'',v.execute('\\\\''select seq,publication_day,call_id from judgements where view_id=? and seq>=? order by seq limit 1'\\\\'',(k,starts[k])).fetchone(),'\\\\''settled price'\\\\'',round(cost,6))\nprint('\\\\''retired original refusal rows:'\\\\'',[(c,k,round(cost,6)) for c,k,sha,cost in refused if k in starts],'\\\\''all refused:'\\\\'',[(c,k) for c,k,sha,cost in refused])\nprint('\\\\''base per sequence'\\\\'',total,'\\\\''6x'\\\\'',total*6,'\\\\''median reserve'\\\\'',statistics.median(reserve),'\\\\''max'\\\\'',max(reserve),'\\\\''median sec'\\\\'',statistics.median(seconds),'\\\\''avg sec'\\\\'',statistics.mean(seconds))\nfor d,r,t in [('\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v8'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-26'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-26'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'')]:\n miss=sorted({day for day in dates[r] if day>=d} - set(dates[t]))\n print('\\\\''historic reader-only judgement days'\\\\'',r,t,len(miss),miss[:6])\nfor variant in (1,2,3):\n active={k:set(x[0] for x in ls) for k,ls in attempts.items()}\n active['\\\\''v14'\\\\''].update(day for day,chg in dates['\\\\''v8'\\\\''].items() if chg and day>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'')\n active['\\\\''v9'\\\\''].update(day for day in active['\\\\''v14'\\\\''] if day>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'')\n active['\\\\''v16'\\\\''].update(day for day in active['\\\\''v14'\\\\''] if day>='\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\'')\n if variant==3: active['\\\\''v16'\\\\''].update(day for day,chg in dates['\\\\''v8'\\\\''].items() if chg and day>='\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\'')\n active['\\\\''v21'\\\\''].update(day for day in active['\\\\''v16'\\\\'']| (active['\\\\''v9'\\\\''] if variant>1 else set()) if day>='\\\\''2026-07-26'\\\\'')\n print('\\\\''extra days if every fresh reader marks changed'\\\\'',variant,{k:len(active[k])-len(ls) for k,ls in attempts.items()})\nprint('\\\\''July12 outcomes'\\\\'',cases['\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\''])\nfor d in ('\\\\''2026-08-13'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-14'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-18'\\\\''):\n print(d,cases[d])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections as co, json, math, pathlib, re, sqlite3, statistics\nimport window_test as w\nfrom hivemind import config, model\nroot=w.REPO\ndef sql(path): return sqlite3.connect(path.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nv=sql(w.OLD2/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\na=sql(w.OLD2/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'')\nstarts={'\\\\''v9'\\\\'':148,'\\\\''v14'\\\\'':148,'\\\\''v16'\\\\'':265,'\\\\''v21'\\\\'':534}\npr=w.july_test.budget_module()\nrefused=[]\nattempts={k:[] for k in starts}\ndates={k:{} for k in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'',*starts)}\ncases=co.defaultdict(dict)\nfor view,seq,d,change,call,sha,out in v.execute('\\\\''select view_id, seq, publication_day, changed, call_id, request_sha256, implied_outcome from judgements order by judgement_id'\\\\''):\n if view not in dates: continue\n dates[view][d]=bool(change)\n if view in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'') and d>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'': cases[d][view]=out\n if view in starts and seq>=starts[view]:\n    r=a.execute('\\\\''select call_id, request_json,response_json,seconds from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call,)).fetchone()\n    assert a.execute('\\\\''select request_sha256 from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call,)).fetchone()[0]==sha\n    attempts[view].append((d,*r))\nfor c,sha,req,res,sec in a.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_sha256,request_json,response_json,seconds from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\'' and (request_sha256 like '\\\\''%:refused:%'\\\\'' or request_sha256 like '\\\\''%:schema:%'\\\\'')\\\"):\n rr=json.loads(req)\n refused.append((c,w.july_test.judged_view(rr),sha,pr.llm_cost(json.loads(res),rr)))\ntotal=0; reserve=[]; seconds=[]\nfor k,ls in attempts.items():\n cost=sum(pr.llm_cost(json.loads(res),json.loads(req)) for d,c,req,res,sec in ls)\n total+=cost\n reserve.extend(pr.llm_estimate(json.loads(req)) for d,c,req,res,sec in ls)\n seconds.extend(sec for d,c,req,res,sec in ls)\n print(k,len(ls),'\\\\''first seq/day/call'\\\\'',v.execute('\\\\''select seq,publication_day,call_id from judgements where view_id=? and seq>=? order by seq limit 1'\\\\'',(k,starts[k])).fetchone(),'\\\\''settled price'\\\\'',round(cost,6))\nprint('\\\\''retired original refusal rows:'\\\\'',[(c,k,round(cost,6)) for c,k,sha,cost in refused if k in starts],'\\\\''all refused:'\\\\'',[(c,k) for c,k,sha,cost in refused])\nprint('\\\\''base per sequence'\\\\'',total,'\\\\''6x'\\\\'',total*6,'\\\\''median reserve'\\\\'',statistics.median(reserve),'\\\\''max'\\\\'',max(reserve),'\\\\''median sec'\\\\'',statistics.median(seconds),'\\\\''avg sec'\\\\'',statistics.mean(seconds))\nfor d,r,t in [('\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v8'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-26'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\''),('\\\\''2026-07-26'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'')]:\n miss=sorted({day for day in dates[r] if day>=d} - set(dates[t]))\n print('\\\\''historic reader-only judgement days'\\\\'',r,t,len(miss),miss[:6])\nfor variant in (1,2,3):\n active={k:set(x[0] for x in ls) for k,ls in attempts.items()}\n active['\\\\''v14'\\\\''].update(day for day,chg in dates['\\\\''v8'\\\\''].items() if chg and day>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'')\n active['\\\\''v9'\\\\''].update(day for day in active['\\\\''v14'\\\\''] if day>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'')\n active['\\\\''v16'\\\\''].update(day for day in active['\\\\''v14'\\\\''] if day>='\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\'')\n if variant==3: active['\\\\''v16'\\\\''].update(day for day,chg in dates['\\\\''v8'\\\\''].items() if chg and day>='\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\'')\n active['\\\\''v21'\\\\''].update(day for day in active['\\\\''v16'\\\\'']| (active['\\\\''v9'\\\\''] if variant>1 else set()) if day>='\\\\''2026-07-26'\\\\'')\n print('\\\\''extra days if every fresh reader marks changed'\\\\'',variant,{k:len(active[k])-len(ls) for k,ls in attempts.items()})\nprint('\\\\''July12 outcomes'\\\\'',cases['\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\''])\nfor d in ('\\\\''2026-08-13'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-14'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-18'\\\\''):\n print(d,cases[d])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"v9 70 first seq/day/call (167, '2026-07-10', 444) settled price 0.310231\nv14 71 first seq/day/call (167, '2026-07-10', 439) settled price 0.283985\nv16 56 first seq/day/call (274, '2026-07-15', 849) settled price 0.146312\nv21 50 first seq/day/call (542, '2026-07-26', 1776) settled price 0.131619\nretired original refusal rows: [] all refused: [(591, 'v7'), (6955, 'v34'), (7068, 'v35'), (7774, 'v35')]\nbase per sequence 0.872147715 6x 5.23288629 median reserve 0.0194724 max 0.0429802 median sec 38.2 avg sec 39.35748987854251\nhistoric reader-only judgement days v14 v8 10 ['2026-07-11', '2026-07-18', '2026-08-04', '2026-08-05', '2026-08-08', '2026-08-12']\nhistoric reader-only judgement days v9 v14 1 ['2026-07-19']\nhistoric reader-only judgement days v16 v14 0 []\nhistoric reader-only judgement days v21 v16 3 ['2026-08-02', '2026-08-12', '2026-09-06']\nhistoric reader-only judgement days v21 v9 1 ['2026-08-02']\nextra days if every fresh reader marks changed 1 {'v9': 2, 'v14': 0, 'v16': 10, 'v21': 7}\nextra days if every fresh reader marks changed 2 {'v9': 2, 'v14': 0, 'v16': 10, 'v21': 7}\nextra days if every fresh reader marks changed 3 {'v9': 2, 'v14': 0, 'v16': 10, 'v21': 7}\nJuly12 outcomes {'v14': 'About $387 billion: starting with Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of approximately $91 billion, I carry the roughly 11.5% sequential increase forward to Q3 and Q4. This remains within rung 3 and below $400 billion.', 'v9': 'About $400–410B of FY2027 Data Center revenue. I use the Q1 $75.25B result and Q2 growth outlook as the operating base, then give partial—not full—weight to the roughly $1T Blackwell/Vera Rubin visibility across calendar 2026–27 because it spans multiple periods and products; the discounted estimate is just above the $400B rung boundary.'}\n2026-08-13 {'v14': 'About $392 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 actual + $91.0 billion Q2 guidance + $103.1 billion Q3 analyst expectation + about $116.7 billion for Q4, carrying the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate forward once.', 'v9': \"About $440B for FY2027: the carried-forward trajectory, Q1's $75.25B result, Q2's $91B total-revenue guide with stated Data Center growth acceleration, and the quantified H2 tracking upside support an annual outcome above the reference. The longer-horizon Blackwell/Rubin and SpaceX figures are discounted for timing and for the absence of sized FY2027 NVIDIA shipments.\"}\n2026-09-14 {'v14': 'About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1, $96.2 billion in Q2, and $108 billion at the Q3 guidance midpoint, plus an estimated $121.3 billion in Q4 by extending the roughly 12.3% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate. This is above $400 billion and below $450 billion.', 'v9': 'Approximately $414 billion: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total about $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100 billion of Data Center revenue at the latest reported mix. Carrying forward the prior H2 baseline of about $208 billion and applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% above-estimates forecast gives about $249.6 billion for H2, including Q3, and about $414 billion for FY2027.'}\n2026-09-18 {'v14': \"About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 reported revenue total $177.8 billion; the $108 billion Q3 guide, adjusted toward the $113–114 billion analyst estimate and the recent 3.1% average beat of guidance's high end, implies roughly $113.6 billion for Q3. Carrying approximately 12% sequential growth into Q4 implies about $127.2 billion, for approximately $418.6 billion across FY2027.\", 'v9': 'About $379–384 billion: roughly $164 billion in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 based on the $108 billion total-revenue guidance and recent Data Center mix, and approximately $115–120 billion in Q4 as hyperscale growth reaccelerates and Rubin supply builds.'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
