{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '117,140p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '234,275p'; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '227,235p'; rg -n 'D696 ·|D699 ·|D705 ·' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba codex-r20.md | tail -16\"","aggregated_output":"   117\t        if finished != len(to_run):\n   118\t            raise RuntimeError('day runner did not complete every routed item')\n   119\t        seq = store.next_sequence(conn) - 1\n   120\t        judged = round_module.judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, transport=transport, log=log)\n   121\t        day_stats['judged'] += judged.judged\n   122\t        day_stats['changed'] += judged.changed\n   123\t        if judged.failed:\n   124\t            day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   125\t            log(f'  ! day judging: {judged.failed}')\n   126\t            raise RuntimeError(f'judging failed; day {day} remains resumable: {judged.failed}')\n   127\t        closed = pull.end_of_day(conn, day, seq)\n   128\t        day_stats['closed'] = len(closed)\n   129\t        # The day ends at the last sequence it wrote, a closing's own sequence on a day without items included, so the next day starts after it.\n   130\t        store.complete_day(conn, day, store.next_sequence(conn) - 1, time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   131\t        conn.commit()\n   132\t        for key in totals:\n   133\t            totals[key] += day_stats[key]\n   134\t        calls, cost, _, _ = archive.totals()\n   135\t        day_cost = cost - day_cost_before  # Includes discarded speculative calls and repaired refusals.\n   136\t        open_count = len(store.open_views(conn))\n   137\t        log(f'{day} | items {day_stats[\"items\"]:3d} extracted {day_stats[\"extracted\"]:3d} merged {day_stats[\"merged\"]:2d} skipped {day_stats[\"not_processed\"]:2d} '\n   138\t            f'failed {day_stats[\"failed\"]:2d} | evidence {day_stats[\"evidence\"]:3d} new views {day_stats[\"new_views\"]:2d} judged {day_stats[\"judged\"]:3d} '\n   139\t            f'changed {day_stats[\"changed\"]:3d} closed {len(closed)} | open views {open_count} | day ${day_cost:.2f} total ${cost - cost_before:.2f} calls {calls - calls_before}')\n   140\t        if day0 and day == day0:\n   234\tdef current_state(conn, view_id):\n   235\t    \"\"\"The latest judgement: rung, reasons, changed, seq and day, and its reference and implied outcome (D260) where the ledger has them.\"\"\"\n   236\t    columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(judgements)')}\n   237\t    stance = ''.join(f', {field}' for field in ('reference', 'implied_outcome') if field in columns)\n   238\t    row = conn.execute(f'select judgement_id, rung, reasons, changed, seq, publication_day{stance} from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   239\t    return dict(row) if row else None\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\tdef dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n   243\t    \"\"\"Each dependency with its current target: the resolved view, or the waiting chain and year.\"\"\"\n   244\t    out = []\n   245\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\n   246\t        dep = dict(dep)\n   247\t        resolution = conn.execute('select resolved_to, reason from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\n   248\t        if resolution:\n   249\t            dep['resolved_to'], dep['resolution'] = resolution['resolved_to'], resolution['reason']\n   250\t        else:\n   251\t            dep['resolved_to'], dep['resolution'] = dep['depends_on'], ('direct' if dep['depends_on'] else 'waiting')\n   252\t        out.append(dep)\n   253\t    return out\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef direct_parents(conn, view_id, seq=None):\n   257\t    \"\"\"The views this view depends on directly (a driver's root, D208; the seeds' depends_on), written at or before `seq` when given.\n   258\t    The filing reads it to keep a statement under the narrower of two linked questions (D207's narrowest rule, extraction.file_reading).\"\"\"\n   259\t    reads = \" and coalesce(kind, '') != 'reads'\" if 'kind' in {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(dependencies)')} else ''\n   260\t    rows = conn.execute(f\"select depends_on from dependencies where view_id=? and depends_on != '' and (? is null or seq <= ?){reads} order by dependency_id\", (view_id, seq, seq))\n   261\t    return list(dict.fromkeys(r[0] for r in rows))\n   262\t\n   263\t\n   264\tdef dependants_of(conn, view_id):\n   265\t    direct = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,))]\n   266\t    resolved = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute(\n   267\t        'select d.view_id from dependency_resolutions r join dependencies d on d.dependency_id=r.dependency_id where r.resolved_to=?', (view_id,))]\n   268\t    return sorted(set(direct + resolved))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\tdef would_cycle(conn, view_id, depends_on):\n   272\t    \"\"\"True when depends_on already depends, directly or through its dependencies, on view_id.\"\"\"\n   273\t    seen, stack = set(), [depends_on]\n   274\t    while stack:\n   275\t        current = stack.pop()\n   227\tdef llm_estimate(request):\n   228\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   229\t    cap = request.get('max_completion_tokens', request.get('max_tokens'))\n   230\t    if isinstance(cap, bool) or not isinstance(cap, int) or cap <= 0:\n   231\t        raise model.TransportError('request without a positive output cap: refused by the budget')\n   232\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   233\t    return (tokens_in * price_in + cap * price_out) / 1e6\n   234\t\n   235\t\n10467:## D696 · 2026-11-21 · Alex keeps the July test's $0.15 limit as a reservation stop priced from each request's size\n10505:## D699 · 2026-11-21 · Alex continues with A: the whole-window measurement of the linking version, designed with the council at $0 first\n10583:## D705 · 2026-11-21 · The version-2 link question passes its registered gate; council R: version 2 goes to the paid design\n     6\t\n     7\t### 2. The new July link is weak\n     8\t\n     9\tI agree with Claude’s inventory. The two unsupported links disappeared, two defensible links disappeared, and the `v21–v9` reversal did not recur. The known positive still had a margin below 0.10 in two draws. One qualification: the probe changed three pieces of wording together. The results establish which links changed, while the effect of each sentence remains unmeasured. For the defensible `v35 reads v14` link, two V2 draws still favoured that direction below the threshold. [Claude’s read](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/claude-r20.md:3) · [Current-wording table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/census-pairs.md:20) · [V2 table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-pairs.md:84)\n    10\t\n    11\t**`v14 reads v8` is weak, with plausible downstream harm.** The seq-148 request gave the total a direct **$393B FY2027** estimate. The CPU card showed its ladder and Intel and AMD market shares. It supplied no full-year NVIDIA CPU forecast in the evidence shown to the matcher. If both directions would help, the tie-break favours the CPU question reading the total. The broad total also gives the CPU question little useful constraint, so `neither` is defensible. The positive sign is arithmetically plausible if other sales hold fixed. The risk is that the total treats an uncertain CPU forecast as incremental to a company estimate that may already include those sales. The probe bought no judgements, so that harm remains unmeasured. [Seq-148 request record, archive call 8741](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/probe-v2-1/census.json:455) · [Evidence shown to the matcher](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) · [Tie-break](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:16)\n    12\t\n    13\t### 3. One next step\n    14\t\n    15\t**Choose (a).** Put the tested wording into a separately versioned, reviewed product configuration, then design the paid comparison. A third wording could improve the CPU decision or recover the two lost links. Choosing it by performance on these same 105 pairs would be selection on the probe set, so those pairs could diagnose the change but could no longer independently validate that choice. Returning to the current wording avoids the new CPU link and keeps the two defensible links, while bringing back the known base-effect error. Stopping saves the judgement spend and leaves the product question unanswered. The eventual send still needs the design pass and Alex’s ceiling. [Registered next step](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:53) · [Iteration rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:326) · [D699](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10505)\n    16\t\n    17\t### 4. Keep the full chain and read it one step at a time\n    18\t\n    19\tIn each linked sequence, commit both seq-148 links. First prove at $0 that the product version reproduces its paired probe request hashes and graph. Replay `v8` by exact request identity wherever its inputs are unchanged. Let production judge `v14` before `v9` when both are due. In each paired no-link control, sample both `v14` and `v9` fresh from their first affected judgement onward, without forcing extra control judgement days. [Paired control design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:153) · [Judgement order](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:305)\n    20\t\n    21\tFor each common date, show **which CPU conclusion the linked total saw, how that total compares with its fresh control, and which exact total Data Center saw**. Judge Data Center against its own sequence’s available total. Report days added by propagation separately. Credit reconciliation only when the forecasts still have sound arithmetic and sourcing. Moving the whole to accommodate the part would be visible in the `v14` comparison. This measures the full V2 chain. The original July test remains the separate evidence for the single Data Center link. [Dependency block](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:127) · [Propagation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:350) · [July reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md:5)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
