{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def end_of_day|def close|current_state|judgement' ../../../src/hivemind/pull.py; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/pull.py | sed -n '70,131p'; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10467,10480p'; nl -ba window_test.py | sed -n '43,48p;69,78p;434,447p'\"","aggregated_output":"12:    last = conn.execute('select rung from judgements where view_id=? order by seq desc, judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n14:        return f'due {due_day}, closed on {day} with no judgement: {NO_DATA}'\n30:def end_of_day(conn, day, seq):\n 10467\t## D696 · 2026-11-21 · Alex keeps the July test's $0.15 limit as a reservation stop priced from each request's size\n 10468\t\n 10469\t- **The question** (after council R round 11, `docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r11.md`): the budget\n 10470\t  transport reserves, before each model call, a worst case priced from the request's size (2 x its bytes + 4,096 input tokens, the full\n 10471\t  output cap) and refuses a call that would pass $0.15. Over 6,853 stored calls the charge never passed 31% of that reservation, but\n 10472\t  OpenAI publishes no bound tying a request's tokens to its size; its only published input bound (922,000 tokens) would reserve about\n 10473\t  $0.12 a call and make the test impossible under $0.15. Expected total about $0.09. Options: reserve from the request's size\n 10474\t  (recommended); or do not run.\n 10475\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"按请求长度预扣 (推荐)\".\n 10476\t- **Also fixed on council R's round-11 finding** (verified against the stored usage and the published pricing page, read 2026-11-21):\n 10477\t  gpt-6-luna bills cache writes at $0.125 per million tokens (1.25x input); every stored judge response reports `cache_write_tokens`.\n 10478\t  The July harness settles at the three published input rates (`july_test.settled_llm_cost`: the stored 07-10 Data Center call $0.002895,\n 10479\t  not $0.002662) and reserves each Jev request at TypeSafe's published 64K per-request limit for each of its three attempts. The\n 10480\t  product's own `model.call` cost records omit the cache-write premium too: a cost-reporting finding, recorded, not changed here.\n    43\t    \"\"\"old-2's answers its own run refused (the archive keeps them under the request's hash with a ':refused:' suffix, so no later\n    44\t    identical request is answered with them): {request hash: stored provider response}. A replay must meet each refusal again to\n    45\t    reach the stored retry.\"\"\"\n    46\t    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    47\t    return {sha.split(':refused:')[0]: json.loads(response) for sha, response in\n    48\t            stored.execute(\"select request_sha256, response_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:refused:%' order by call_id\")}\n    69\t    def transport(*args):\n    70\t        if len(args) == 1 and july_test.is_link_request(args[0]):\n    71\t            asked.append(sorted(args[0]['questions']))\n    72\t            return link_answer(args[0])\n    73\t        response = stored_refusals.pop(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1], None)\n    74\t        if response is not None:                   # old-2's own run refused this answer: give it back, so the check refuses it again\n    75\t            refused_again.append(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1][:12])\n    76\t            return response\n    77\t        (folder / 'missed-request.json').write_text(json.dumps(args[-1], ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n    78\t        raise july_test.Stop('a request other than a link question missed the archive')\n   434\t    command, scratch = sys.argv[1], Path(sys.argv[2])\n   435\t    if command == 'neither':\n   436\t        sys.exit(0 if neither(scratch) else 1)\n   437\t    if command == 'census-dry':\n   438\t        sys.exit(0 if census_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   439\t    if command == 'census-reuse-dry':\n   440\t        sys.exit(0 if census_reuse_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   441\t    if command == 'reuse-refusals':\n   442\t        sys.exit(0 if reuse_refusals(scratch) else 1)\n   443\t    if command == 'v120-replay':\n   444\t        sys.exit(0 if v120_replay(scratch, sys.argv[3]) else 1)\n   445\t    if command in ('probe-v2-dry', 'probe-v2'):\n   446\t        raise SystemExit(RETIRED_PROBE)\n   447\t    if command == 'census':\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/pull.py | sed -n '1,55p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '125,166p'; nl -ba ../../../docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '129,135p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/pull.py | sed -n '1,55p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '125,166p'; nl -ba ../../../docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '129,135p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"Pull mode (D54, D356): at the end of a day (the day passed in, never read from a clock), every open view whose due day has come\n     2\tis frozen where its state stands and closed. The closing record names the rung it froze at; a view that was never judged closes\n     3\twith \"no data to verify\" (AGENTS §8: missing data is neither a pass nor a fail). Nothing waits for the day's items, there is no\n     4\tseparate final review, and no other question is re-judged here.\"\"\"\n     5\tfrom . import dispatch\n     6\tfrom .views import store\n     7\t\n     8\tNO_DATA = 'no data to verify'\n     9\t\n    10\t\n    11\tdef closing_reason(conn, view_id, due_day, day):\n    12\t    last = conn.execute('select rung from judgements where view_id=? order by seq desc, judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n    13\t    if last is None:\n    14\t        return f'due {due_day}, closed on {day} with no judgement: {NO_DATA}'\n    15\t    label = conn.execute('select label from rungs where view_id=? and position=?', (view_id, last['rung'])).fetchone()\n    16\t    return f'due {due_day}, frozen on {day} at rung {last[\"rung\"]} {label[\"label\"] if label else \"\"}'.rstrip()\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef closing_sequence(conn, day, seq):\n    20\t    \"\"\"The sequence number the day's closings are written under, so that they are dated on that day: the day's last number when\n    21\t    the day wrote it, else a new one recorded as the day's own step (a day with no items would otherwise date them on the day before).\"\"\"\n    22\t    row = conn.execute('select min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no=?', (seq,)).fetchone()\n    23\t    if seq > 0 and row[0] == day:\n    24\t        return seq\n    25\t    own = max(store.next_sequence(conn), seq + 1)\n    26\t    dispatch.mark(conn, {'input_id': f'day:{day}', 'publication_day': day}, own, 'closed', 'ok', 'due questions closed at the end of the day')\n    27\t    return own\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef end_of_day(conn, day, seq):\n    31\t    due = [row for row in conn.execute('select view_id, due_day from views where due_day <= ? order by created_seq', (day,)).fetchall()\n    32\t           if store.is_open(conn, row['view_id'])]\n    33\t    if due:\n    34\t        seq = closing_sequence(conn, day, seq)\n    35\t    for row in due:\n    36\t        store.close_view(conn, row['view_id'], closing_reason(conn, row['view_id'], row['due_day'], day), 'pull', seq)\n    37\t    conn.commit()\n    38\t    return [row['view_id'] for row in due]\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\tdef _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag):\n   128\t    \"\"\"judging-v8 (D694, design §3): the read judgement's comparison point and the system's forecast in full, labelled as ours, beside\n   129\t    the reasons excerpt; the read question not judged yet shows only that.\"\"\"\n   130\t    if not state:\n   131\t        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now not judged yet']\n   132\t    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}',\n   133\t            f'    Comparison point stated by that judgement: {_indented(state.get(\"reference\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   134\t            f'    The system\\'s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): {_indented(state.get(\"implied_outcome\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   135\t            f'    Reasons (excerpt): {_indented((state.get(\"reasons\") or \"\")[:600])}']\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0, full_dependencies=False):\n   139\t    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown. full_dependencies: the judging-v8 dependency block.\"\"\"\n   140\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n   141\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n   142\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n   143\t    if hidden:\n   144\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n   145\t    for p in pieces:\n   146\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   147\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   148\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   149\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   150\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   151\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   152\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   153\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   154\t    if deps:\n   155\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   156\t        for d in deps:\n   157\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   158\t            if not target:\n   159\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   160\t                continue\n   161\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   162\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   163\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   164\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   165\t            if full_dependencies:\n   166\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   129\t- Theme theses do not judge outcomes as good or bad. Each dependent asset thesis records its direction: rate cuts are bullish for Ethereum and bearish for JPM.\n   130\t- A dependency has one direction. An apparent “good first, bad later” relationship needs an intermediate thesis: steel tariffs raising domestic steel prices and weakening downstream steel demand are separate paths.\n   131\t- Dependencies and the theme block are the two ways theses influence each other; succession only orders periods. B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion. The theme block (D191, D195) shows every open, judged theme thesis to every asset thesis's judgement, one to all, and the judgement states which way each theme it weighed pushes it; no edge is written for it. Keep B's direct evidence separate from dependency states and reasons. A's conclusion can affect B like evidence but is not stored as evidence: external events and statements are evidence, whereas A is our own judgement. Treating it as evidence would let the system convince itself.\n   132\t- Count a statement once. A statement about A is A's evidence, including when two candidates arise from one item. B learns it through A's conclusion. Daily filing gives a statement one home: the narrowest open thesis it bears on, as that thesis's own figure, step or estimate or through the demand, supply, competition or pricing behind its answer, plus the same answer's candidates (D207, D259, D264, D265); the separate coverage-start reading was retired (D370). Dependencies are chosen only when B is created; a later item adding a dependency to an existing thesis is decided (D191 point 2) and to be built (D368).\n   133\t- Rejudge an open thesis when its inputs change: new evidence, replacement, a new link to existing evidence, a dependency declaring a changed conclusion, or (for an asset thesis) a theme thesis declaring one. Additional source references alone do not count. Binding an awaited A or moving to its successor also changes B's inputs. Closed theses do not update. A memo-derived thesis is first judged when evidence first links to it; before that, it and its dependants see “not yet judged”.\n   134\t- The matching call chooses a new thesis's dependencies, stating which conclusions it relies on and each direction (D51). Choose only among searched theses, extraction block-5 theses and candidates opened from the same item; no extra search. Jev, the default matcher, is not asked for them, so new theses do not receive dependencies through the default matcher; building the choice on the Jev path is decided (D368). The historical seed questions are retired (D370). A historical seed's dependency arrow means \"supports\" (D368, by D208): for filing, the supporting (driver) thesis is the narrower one; for judging, the supported (root) thesis reads the supporting theses' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged before their roots. The judging code reads the stored edge the other way today; the fix is to be built and measured (D368). Completed events are evidence, not dependencies: today's oil price influencing OPEC output is evidence for the OPEC-output thesis.\n   135\t- Before adding an edge or following it to a successor, code checks for cycles. Refuse a cycle and ask the model to correct it; persistent cycles follow normal failure handling. Apparently mutually dependent questions indicate poorly defined theses.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
