{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'succession|resolve|depend' ../../../src/hivemind/views/writing.py | head -35; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '111,131p;168,217p'; nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '297,322p'\"","aggregated_output":"3:was said (a later-arriving older statement is logged, not linked); a revised piece still linked elsewhere links the new piece there too; new views come with rungs, dependencies and\n4:successions; a waiting dependency is resolved when the chain's year is created; the set of views whose reading\n40:    # the year is stored in its one canonical spelling so that a waiting dependency's year joins it (D163 plan, period text)\n50:def resolve_waiting(conn, new_view_id, seq, changed):\n51:    \"\"\"A new view on a chain satisfies dependencies waiting for its year on that chain.\"\"\"\n57:        for row in conn.execute('select succeeds from successions where view_id=?', (current,)):\n61:    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where wait_year=? and wait_chain_view_id is not null', (v['year'],)):\n63:            already = conn.execute('select 1 from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=?', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\n65:                store.insert(conn, 'dependency_resolutions', dependency_id=dep['dependency_id'], resolved_to=new_view_id, reason='created', seq=seq)\n70:    return universe.resolve(candidate['object']) or candidate['object']\n133:    \"\"\"D694, D695 (design §4): each proposed link resolved to stored ids, re-checked against the ledger as it stands inside this write\n148:        existing = {r['direction'] for r in conn.execute('select direction from dependencies where view_id=? and depends_on=?', (reader, read))}\n155:        store.insert(conn, 'dependencies', view_id=reader, depends_on=read, wait_chain_view_id='', wait_year='', direction=label, seq=seq, kind=_links.KIND)\n175:        if outcome not in ('new', 'succession'):\n183:        object_id = universe.resolve(c['object'])\n184:        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n189:        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n190:            store.insert(conn, 'successions', view_id=view_id, succeeds=target, seq=seq)\n209:    # 2. dependencies of the new views (candidate ids resolve to the views just created)\n210:    dependencies_written = set()\n217:            depends_on = dep['view_id']\n218:            if depends_on in new_views:\n219:                depends_on = new_views[depends_on]\n220:            elif depends_on in candidate_ids:\n221:                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> candidate {depends_on} dropped: that candidate was not opened')\n223:            if depends_on and store.would_cycle(conn, view_id, depends_on):\n224:                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> {depends_on} dropped: cycle')\n233:            edge = (view_id, depends_on, chain, wait_year, dep['direction'])\n234:            if edge in dependencies_written:\n236:            dependencies_written.add(edge)\n237:            store.insert(conn, 'dependencies', view_id=view_id, depends_on=depends_on, wait_chain_view_id=chain, wait_year=wait_year,\n239:        resolve_waiting(conn, view_id, seq, changed)\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\tdef write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass, *, proposed_links=None):\n   114\t    \"\"\"Write atomically within the caller's transaction; the caller commits the completion marker with it. proposed_links: the reading\n   115\t    links the link step chose (views/links.py, D694), written after the new views exist; None writes none.\"\"\"\n   116\t    if not conn.in_transaction:\n   117\t        conn.execute('begin immediate')\n   118\t    conn.execute('savepoint view_write')\n   119\t    try:\n   120\t        store.ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n   121\t        result = _write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   122\t        if proposed_links:\n   123\t            result.links = _write_links(conn, seq, proposed_links, result)\n   124\t    except Exception:\n   125\t        conn.execute('rollback to view_write')\n   126\t        conn.execute('release view_write')\n   127\t        raise\n   128\t    conn.execute('release view_write')\n   129\t    return result\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   168\t    if problems:\n   169\t        raise WriteConflict('; '.join(problems))\n   170\t    created = {}\n   171\t    # 1. new views, themes first\n   172\t    order = sorted(handover.candidates, key=lambda c: 0 if c['kind'] == 'theme' else 1)\n   173\t    for c in order:\n   174\t        outcome, target, deps = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   175\t        if outcome not in ('new', 'succession'):\n   176\t            continue\n   177\t        canonical = aliases[c['id']]\n   178\t        if canonical in created:\n   179\t            new_views[c['id']] = created[canonical]\n   180\t            continue\n   181\t        if store.exact_key_views(conn, c):\n   182\t            raise WriteConflict(f'candidate {c[\"id\"]}: existing exact identity requires matching')\n   183\t        object_id = universe.resolve(c['object'])\n   184\t        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n   185\t            c = oriented_like(c, store.rungs_of(conn, target), notes)\n   186\t        view_id = _create_view(conn, c, object_id, universe.kind(object_id), seq, item, universe)\n   187\t        new_views[c['id']] = view_id\n   188\t        created[canonical] = view_id\n   189\t        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n   190\t            store.insert(conn, 'successions', view_id=view_id, succeeds=target, seq=seq)\n   191\t        changed.add(view_id)\n   192\t    # 1b. research groups (D149, D165, D166): the groups module plans creations and memberships from the handover's\n   193\t    #     declarations, the stored groups' names and each new thesis's own text; a merged candidate adds nothing\n   194\t    from .. import extraction as _extraction\n   195\t    from . import groups as _groups\n   196\t    creations, memberships, group_notes, extensions = _groups.plan(getattr(handover, 'new_groups', None) or [], _groups.stored_groups(conn), order, new_views,\n   197\t                                                                    _extraction.tracks_a_matter, universe)\n   198\t    notes.extend(group_notes)\n   199\t    group_ids = {}\n   200\t    for creation in creations:\n   201\t        group_ids[creation['local_id']] = _next_id(conn, 'thesis_groups', 'group_id', 'g')\n   202\t        objects = sorted({store.view(conn, view_id)['object_id'] for view_id, key, _ in memberships if key == creation['local_id']})\n   203\t        store.add_group(conn, group_id=group_ids[creation['local_id']], name=creation['name'], scope=creation['scope'], seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'],\n   204\t                        object_ids=objects, aliases=creation['aliases'])\n   205\t    for view_id, key, basis in memberships:\n   206\t        store.add_member(conn, group_ids.get(key, key), view_id, seq, item['input_id'], basis)\n   207\t    for group_id, names in extensions:            # D166: a declaration that is a stored group under other names gives it those names\n   208\t        store.add_group_aliases(conn, group_id, names, seq, item['input_id'])\n   209\t    # 2. dependencies of the new views (candidate ids resolve to the views just created)\n   210\t    dependencies_written = set()\n   211\t    for c in order:\n   212\t        outcome, target, deps = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   213\t        if c['id'] not in new_views:\n   214\t            continue\n   215\t        view_id = new_views[c['id']]\n   216\t        for dep in deps:\n   217\t            depends_on = dep['view_id']\n   297\t  made for another version; scores are compared only on the same gold. Do not write a new scorer to judge a probe: read the traces yourself (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   298\t  \"不要写评分器这个之前就出问题过，你自己读trace 来分析\"). Alex, 2026-10-29 (D244): \"我觉得这是最容易出错的问题；你非常容易写死，我们在改的过程中如果drift你会一直用久的标准来衡量，这边需要有打分，但是“一定”要你自己下去看trace这是必须，记起来\".\n   299\t- **The ruler counts only what it was built to count.** Before a quality claim, a reader who did not write the change also reads the\n   300\t  fields the product stores (original day, original speaker, tier, the summary's hedges) and what the next step does with the record\n   301\t  (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"现在到底质量怎么样你深度的解析不要只是看尺子\").\n   302\t- Read the judges' reasons, not only the scores, and pick the next fix from the largest cause. Open the samples behind a metric's largest\n   303\t  values before reading it, and write down what a derived number reduces to.\n   304\t- **Report every number, regressions first.** For future evidence evaluation, combine the existing gold's core and supporting entries as helpful, use its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral (D372). Count one research matter in one article (D250), not raw sentences. Retain the old labels and scores in historical results, and do not silently relabel the frozen gold. One quantity per table column. A comparison of\n   305\t  totals uses three draws; a count from one draw is labelled one draw and shows a mechanism, not a difference between arms. Lead with the\n   306\t  mechanism and the share of its class it explains, then the fix.\n   307\t- **Read what was dropped.** A statement the pipeline drops is thrown away with its reason, never parked on a side list; evaluation\n   308\t  reads the dropped statements by hand, classifies them by the mechanism that would have kept them, and fixes the largest class upstream\n   309\t  (D209: \"if it doesn't matter, just fucking throw it away … if there are false positives that got thrown away … you got to pick it up\").\n   310\t- **Measure end to end before a step's arm, and read the parked designs first.** A step's noise that the next step removes is not the\n   311\t  defect, and a step's recall that the next step throws away is. Before any arm on one step: the production replay through the whole path\n   312\t  on the gold window, the count at the step the product reads, and the decisions on the topic read for a parked fix (Alex, 2026-10-31:\n   313\t  \"make sure we are not going around in circles using wrong ruler and wrong prompts that don't work\"). Before a phase targets one step,\n   314\t  the upside of that step done perfectly is measured where the product is judged: the judge is given the gold's own evidence, built by\n   315\t  the production code, a few sends (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"我很不开心你的失败，为什么，深度多轮检讨记录，想思路突破\").\n   316\t- **Read what was kept against the gold, blind, before the next noise arm.** The not-kept gold entries a version keeps are judged by a\n   317\t  reader who wrote neither the gold nor the prompt, mixed with controls it cannot tell apart; where it parts from the gold, the standard\n   318\t  is unclear or the gold misreads it, and that goes to Alex before any arm counts it as noise (Alex, 2026-10-31: \"你再次重新检查尺子，看看是不是这些留下的还有歧义；然后再思考怎么降低noise\").\n   319\t- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n   320\t  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n   321\t- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n   322\t  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"## Part A — READY\n\nThe loader now accepts `link_questions` only in `matching` under `jev-links`, and only as one of the two exact strings. Omission selects V1. I reran the five rejection cases and the three config mutants in memory, checked both old checksums, and verified that both retired probe commands exit before replay. The value table now records the parallel manifest reader and its existing refusal when the fingerprint changes. [Loader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/config.py:89) · [Tests](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_links.py:374) · [Mutation log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/mutants.log:21) · [Value table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:78) · [Retired commands](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:443)\n\n## Part B — NOT READY\n\nThe paired arms are sound. Four design changes are needed before building.\n\n1. **Use the link date to delimit fresh judgements, and verify what each request actually saw.** The links at seq 148, 265 and 534 first affect judgements at seq **167, 274 and 542**, respectively. Identify the old request families by reader and judgement date, including their first attempts and retries. Call IDs identify archive rows to retire. They do not establish when a judgement became eligible. Require a fresh answer for each eligible reader judgement after its link in both arms, including an exact match to an old request. Later control requests can diverge from old-2 because they carry their own previous answers and citations. The dry proof must check the **latest accepted upstream conclusion available when the request was built**. In old-2, `v14` has ten judgement dates on which `v8` has no same-day judgement. Keep the paired probe graph and the four stored non-reader refusals in the replay. [Arm and retirement rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:24) · [Dry proof](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:47) · [Latest-state lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:154) · [Evidence carried forward](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:42) · [Refusal replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:69)\n\n2. **Make P compare the annual forecasts and define one outcome for every case.** The first-amount parser can pick the wrong figure or discard a range endpoint. The old-2 July 12 Data Center answer says **$400–410B**. The design’s example extracts $410B and §6 says it counts the low end. Freeze the comparison on the same post-link calendar dates, with an explicit carry-forward rule. Count a definite contradiction when the segment’s low endpoint exceeds the company’s high endpoint. Report overlapping ranges and missing or ambiguous annual forecasts separately, with a minimum coverage rule. Validate both flagged and unflagged dates on stored answers. The proposed `1 in 20` assumes six exchangeable ranks. It does not follow from three paired draws, especially with ties and the control floor. I would require improvement in all three paired rates once coverage and the control floor are met. Specify that confirmed material harm fails, insufficient coverage or a budget stop is inconclusive, and a complete eligible comparison missing the improvement bar fails. [Parser and primary rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:10) · [Pass, fail and inconclusive](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:58) · [Parser caveat](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:94)\n\n3. **Make the harm checks cover the ways the chain can appear to improve.** For H4, read **every** post-link `v14` answer against the exact CPU conclusion it received and its paired fresh control. Check its reference, forecast and arithmetic whether or not `v8` is cited. Adding the whole CPU forecast to a company estimate that already includes it is harm. A supported increment over the amount already included is a different case. Record unresolved overlap explicitly. For H3, use keyword hits to guide reading and trace claimed market figures to outside statements of the right scope. The existing `unsourced` scan searches the dependency block, so copying a system forecast can clear it. Give a material arithmetic or sourcing error found in the July-style review an effect on the verdict. Restore the per-link report of relation, direction and sign, with the known weak CPU link disclosed. Finally, separate model refusals from infrastructure stops and give H1 an explicit comparison unit and denominator. [Harm rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:68) · [Reference scan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py:49) · [Per-link review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:167) · [July arithmetic rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md:5)\n\n4. **Keep July’s latch for the first build.** Run all six sequences concurrently, with one paid call at a time per sequence. Moving the inner call outside the lock lets an admitted worker reach the transport, or start an internal retry, after a different worker has closed the local latch. The shared ledger checks the shared stop, while the proposed refusal closes only the local latch. If intra-sequence concurrency is needed, specify which admitted calls can still start, how retries are gated, and how outstanding calls settle before final reporting. Prove those cases with a race test. [Concurrency proposal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:88) · [July latch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:56) · [Transport retries](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:268)\n\n**Allow-list.** I found no legitimate non-reader judgement change on this fixed old-2 trajectory. New links run between numeric assets, filing excludes `reads` rows, and judgement propagation queues the recorded dependants. The theme broadcast applies to changed themes, and the four fresh readers are assets. Keep the hard stop on an unexplained non-reader miss. For H2, compare the request and substantive judgement fields by question and day, since extra reader judgements can shift row IDs and the configuration checksum differs by arm. [Fixed-trajectory boundary](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:18) · [Filing](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:256) · [Judgement propagation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:287)\n\n**Cost.** Repricing the **247** old-2 reader judgements from archived usage gives **$0.872 per sequence**, close to the design’s $0.86. On the fixed schedule, I counted **19 extra judgement days per linked sequence** even if every fresh reader marks its conclusion changed. That is about **8%** more accepted judgements. The $6.8 figure is a planning estimate. Replace the 50% propagation assumption with the dry-run count and price prompt growth, retries, and live reservations separately before asking Alex for the ceiling. [Cost estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:81) · [Settlement formula](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:438) · [Reservation formula](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:227)"}}
